{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless","id":1383665,"title":"V5 armour is useless?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-24T13:17:33-07:00","id":1383665,"title":"V5 armour is useless?","content":"Now, prior editions had plenty of problems with armour. In some ways better than reality (Thick clothes are wonderful) and in other ways far worse (A kevlar vest protects for 3 but a common small pistol <i>starts</i> at 4 damage? The best armour protects for only 5 or 6?)<br /> <br /> I can see why it's like that, even if I don't like the reasoning I can see why it's done, and players still have incentive to obtain armour (providing they're willing to take on those ludicrus dex penalties) <br /> <br /> <br /> But in V5<br /> Armour is functionally paper for vampires. Ok, Maybe it works to take the kick out of incindiary rounds, but a plate carrier filled with steel becomes a cheap fabric shirt so long as it's donned by a vampire. Don't argue that vampires don't need armour because they're tough and undead. That's like saying a castle shouldn't benefit from walls if it's on a hill. It just seems rather unfair and breaks a lot of versmillitude for me. I was wondering if people house rule V5 armour heavily or if you're happy with these 'cinematic' rules. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T18:02:41-07:00","id":1383696,"title":"","content":"Just as a note, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> that you CAN post about things other than how V5 sucks. This a forum for V20 too if you want talk about its products.<br /> <br /> Just a friendly neighborhood suggestion-not-quite-warning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T18:03:52-07:00","id":1383697,"title":"","content":"Eh. Armor in this edition is more like how armor functions, by and large, in real circles; it changes traumatic damage into bruises and scrapes, because the armor absorbs the impact. Bulletproof vests turn pierced organis into massive (but not often life-threatening) bruising; plate male deflects the stabs of a spear or slashes of a sword, but leaves bruising and cracked bones.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't take traumatic, life-threatening injury from things like guns and swords, so it has no real use for them. It would effect a Bite attack though (and downgrade appropriately assuming an armored neck) and other things that the Armor would help protect against like reducing the damage from an incendiary round (as it prevents the flames from getting to the burnable part of the vampire, mostly). A vampire wearing plate mail and hit by a battle axe is going to still get the force multiplier behind the blow, just like a human will, but the axe won't cut through (to use a random example). Conversely, a vampire not wearing armor isn't going to care that the axe just cut his spleen in two, but that human is going to take heavy damage, bleeding and shock from the traumatic damage of getting an axe to the side.<br /> <br /> It's fine within the balance of V5 because V5's system is not the exact same nuts and bolts and prior editions. House ruling it can easily skew the system in unintended ways though; house ruling it to be automatic damage reduction will break down the system, numerically, especially when you get into any characters with Fortitude and Armor (which become functionally invincible unless you always have damage do 1 regardless of reduction). Adding dice modifiers will skew things in the same way that lots of traits higher than 5 skew, with hypercompetency in dodging (and then it becomes another type of functional invincibility).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 04-24-2020, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T20:35:13-07:00","id":1383713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless#post1383665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, prior editions had plenty of problems with armour. In some ways better than reality (Thick clothes are wonderful) and in other ways far worse (A kevlar vest protects for 3 but a common small pistol <i>starts</i> at 4 damage? The best armour protects for only 5 or 6?)<br /> <br /> I can see why it's like that, even if I don't like the reasoning I can see why it's done, and players still have incentive to obtain armour (providing they're willing to take on those ludicrus dex penalties)<br /> <br /> <br /> But in V5<br /> Armour is functionally paper for vampires. Ok, Maybe it works to take the kick out of incindiary rounds, but a plate carrier filled with steel becomes a cheap fabric shirt so long as it's donned by a vampire. Don't argue that vampires don't need armour because they're tough and undead. That's like saying a castle shouldn't benefit from walls if it's on a hill. It just seems rather unfair and breaks a lot of versmillitude for me. I was wondering if people house rule V5 armour heavily or if you're happy with these 'cinematic' rules.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> V5s mechanics don't really try and reflect &quot;realism&quot;, they're balanced against other mechanics in terms of 'game effects'. It will drive you nuts trying to think about it in terms of ' what does this actually look like', its about the numbers and a system that isn't very robust when it comes to house rules.<br /> <br /> Hell, just look at some of the Potence powers and how they work based on two different materials of equal strength being effected or how picking up a weapon nerfs your vampiric strength its for mechanical balance because the mechanics of the system break very easily.<br /> <br /> Perhaps there will be a rework/work arounds in the PG?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T00:00:55-07:00","id":1383727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383697#post1383697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. Armor in this edition is more like how armor functions, by and large, in real circles; it changes traumatic damage into bruises and scrapes, because the armor absorbs the impact. Bulletproof vests turn pierced organis into massive (but not often life-threatening) bruising; plate male deflects the stabs of a spear or slashes of a sword, but leaves bruising and cracked bones.<br /> Vampires don't take traumatic, life-threatening injury from things like guns and swords, so it has no real use for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to underline this part so much. in RL, it hardly matters if you fire one round, or 100 rounds against good, modern armor. If the first bullet won't get through, the other 99 won't either. RL armor isn't RPG chance-of-dice armor - but each bullet results in heavy bruising, exactly the way elmerg mentioned. I amusingly used convert-to-bashing armor as an armor type in my custom oWoD armor writeup because of this, way before V5 got even released.<br /> <br /> So, in a way the new rules are more realistic, and it makes sense why vampires hardly need the armor in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T02:46:02-07:00","id":1383742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383697#post1383697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. Armor in this edition is more like how armor functions, by and large, in real circles; it changes traumatic damage into bruises and scrapes, because the armor absorbs the impact. Bulletproof vests turn pierced organis into massive (but not often life-threatening) bruising; plate male deflects the stabs of a spear or slashes of a sword, but leaves bruising and cracked bones.</div> </div> </div> </div>are you sure?<br /> I don't know about bullet proof vests, but I was under the impression that with plate (with padding), you'd hardly feel the blow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T04:14:38-07:00","id":1383748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383727#post1383727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to underline this part so much. in RL, it hardly matters if you fire one round, or 100 rounds against good, modern armor. If the first bullet won't get through, the other 99 won't either.</div> </div> </div> </div>What?<br /> <br /> Unless you're talking about trying to shoot small arms at vehicular armor, this just isn't the case. Most modern personal armor is built around materials that degrade with each impact. Every time a Kelvar vest stops a bullet, it becomes less effective against the next one. Adding in trauma plates extends things, but those are designed to deform/break so you don't and can't take that many hits before becoming ineffective.<br /> <br /> What you said is the exact opposite of how armor works in reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> RL armor isn't RPG chance-of-dice armor... </div> </div> </div>Sure it is as much as anything else is. Armor doesn't cover 100% of your body, so there's always a chance a bullet strikes an unprotected spot or whatnot.<br /> <br /> The big way that armor in VtM (all of them, even V5) is unrealistic is that armor vs. type of weapon doesn't matter. A standard Kevlar vest might save your life from a bullet, but unless you've added some stab plates to it, a knife will cut through it far more easily than a bullet will.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I amusingly used convert-to-bashing armor as an armor type in my custom oWoD armor writeup because of this, way before V5 got even released. </div> </div> </div>In pre-V5, this wouldn't make armor meaningless like V5's implementation does though. Having armor convert a sword's damage to bashing instead of lethal is still a great bonus for a vampire (probably better than a few soak dice really) since vampires soak bashing way better than they soak lethal, and don't automatically take bashing damage already from a sword.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, in a way the new rules are more realistic, and it makes sense why vampires hardly need the armor in the first place. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that vampires still need bones to move around. If you break a vampire's arm, the vampire can't attack as effectively. Having armor to reduce how much force is imparted to the vampire should help them avoid injuries that can impeded them.<br /> <br /> Vampires might not &quot;need&quot; armor, but there's no logical reason why armor wouldn't help them in a serious fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T05:02:32-07:00","id":1383751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383748#post1383748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What?<br /> <br /> Unless you're talking about trying to shoot small arms at vehicular armor, this just isn't the case. Most modern personal armor is built around materials that degrade with each impact. Every time a Kelvar vest stops a bullet, it becomes less effective against the next one. Adding in trauma plates extends things, but those are designed to deform/break so you don't and can't take that many hits before becoming ineffective.<br /> <br /> What you said is the exact opposite of how armor works in reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it of course deteriorates over time - that's kind of physics - but realistically, it won't matter in a single fight. The armors can take more hits than you ever should take in any encounter - so for the purposes of RPG combat? The V5/damage-to-bashing rules are absolutely fine. I actually included subtle if-damage-was-.higher-than-armor-rating in my custom armor rules that simulates the armor itself deteriorating, just because.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T05:11:37-07:00","id":1383752,"title":"","content":"I must admit to the thought of vampires wearing body armour not really occurring to me in any VTM game I\u2019ve ever run or played in, and was apprehensive of even being able to locate the rule in any timely fashion. Yet, there it was, listed in the index as being on page 304. <br /> <br /> I looked them up, read them through and thought \u201chmmmm...yes, that makes sense\u2019. <br /> <br /> That\u2019s 10 seconds of my life I\u2019ll never get back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T05:19:06-07:00","id":1383753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383748#post1383748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The problem is that vampires still need bones to move around. If you break a vampire's arm, the vampire can't attack as effectively. Having armor to reduce how much force is imparted to the vampire should help them avoid injuries that can impeded them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they? I always just assumed that breaking their bones caused them to move in a much more blatantly unnatural way, since they are corpses animated by magic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T05:28:13-07:00","id":1383754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383753#post1383753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they? I always just assumed that breaking their bones caused them to move in a much more blatantly unnatural way, since they are corpses animated by magic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>they get penalties for injuries, which they can ignore when frenzied/riding the wave,<br /> I never understood how that translated","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T07:27:18-07:00","id":1383765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383742#post1383742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> are you sure?<br /> I don't know about bullet proof vests, but I was under the impression that with plate (with padding), you'd hardly feel the blow</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Plate mail and the padding underneath, as well as all the trappings such as the arming doublet and such might lessen the amount of bruising but it would not stop it completely. And a hard enough blow, given by a person of significant enough strength, the padding would not stop the force of the blow entirely. But instead of having a shattered sternum, you'd have cracked ribs, something survivable and something you can (depending on your stamina and pain tolerance) fight on with. That's the point of having the Agg to Sueprficial conversion. If you're wearing plate and a gambeson, which was a fair standard (ignoring the arming doublet since it was incidental for protection of things like the underarms) , a warhammer blow or a hard pike blow is still going to hurt, but it may not shatter your arm or pierce your abdomen, on the first blow to that spot. Thus changing traumatic damage to more survivable damage.<br /> <br /> But if our litmus test is 'vampires wearing plate mail' when it comes to discussing armor, then we have a vastly different issue (outside of a Dark Ages game).than first thought.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383753#post1383753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they? I always just assumed that breaking their bones caused them to move in a much more blatantly unnatural way, since they are corpses animated by magic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383748#post1383748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires might not &quot;need&quot; armor, but there's no logical reason why armor wouldn't help them in a serious fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said cracked bones; I should have said fractures to be more accurate. Normal humans continue to do stuff all the time with fractures in their bones. When you get to the point where your arm bones are shattered, both a human and a vampire aren't really going to be doing much with that arm. Which is mechanically represented by the Critical Injury and the related penalties. Beyond that, verisimilitude can (and should) be sacrificed for mechanical balance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383754#post1383754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they get penalties for injuries, which they can ignore when frenzied/riding the wave,<br /> I never understood how that translated</div> </div> </div> </div>Normal humans power through a lot of injuries that should keep them down in stress and anger. The Beast is just doing the same thing on a more monstrous scale. It's not an unrealistic concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 04-25-2020, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T10:25:03-07:00","id":1383792,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> <br /> While yes, I loath virtually all fluff changes of V5, the rule changes are actually interesting and worth looking at. Given a strong edit; a few tweaks and the removal of a few problem children, the rules are pretty great. I genuinely think a lot of rules of V5 that I don't like are still indicative of an interesting direction and could definetly go on towards something better than prior editions. <br /> <br /> And I was genuinely curious as to what people have house ruled here. An idea for example: Armour increases the required number of successes to hit a target (1-3) provided your weapon isn't more powerful. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383697#post1383697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. Armor in this edition is more like how armor functions, by and large, in real circles; it changes traumatic damage into bruises and scrapes, because the armor absorbs the impact. Bulletproof vests turn pierced organis into massive (but not often life-threatening) bruising; plate male deflects the stabs of a spear or slashes of a sword, but leaves bruising and cracked bones.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it doesn't though. You're wrong. or at least you've got some correct ideas that've led you to a completely wrong conclusion. Armour isn't some RPG damage reduction, and the kind of weapon will really make a big statement over how much actually gets through an armour. If you slashed at someone wearing mail and gambeson, it'd not cut them at all and maybe, at most, give them a bruise. If they were wearing plate; might as well use a foam weapon. Similarly, whilst a high powered rifle might break a rib if it hit an armour plate, a pistol isn't actually going to inconvenience someone if it hit the same place. It's entirely possible for modern armour to entirely negate the force of a weapon. V5 is not a more accurate simulation in this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires don't take traumatic, life-threatening injury from things like guns and swords, so it has no real use for them. <br /> . </div> </div> </div>Getting disembowled is still inconvenient, even if you don't need those organs to live. Having your muscles shredded, losing limbs or your head. What's better than having 'superficial' damage? No damage at all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T10:55:13-07:00","id":1383797,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> <br /> <br /> Just taking a note that you may want to even it up a bit. Maybe a post about something other than negativity for every one that is.<br /> <br /> Just being helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T13:37:33-07:00","id":1383835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383751#post1383751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it of course deteriorates over time - that's kind of physics - but realistically, it won't matter in a single fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it will. There isn't a single personal body armor on sale to the public or to armed forces that can legally claim their armor will not degrade from a single strike; even one of a caliber/charge well below what the armor is rated to protect against.<br /> <br /> There's also no such things as &quot;bulletproof&quot; armor, as there's no modern body armor that has a 100% rate at stopping bullet; even, again, bullet below their rating.<br /> <br /> IRL, having compromised armor is still better than no armor, but modern body armor is compromised extremely easily.<br /> <br /> I have no idea where you're getting the idea that this is something that is beyond the resolution of RPG combat when every ballistics expert in the world would say that one strike is all it takes to compromise armor.<br /> <br /> That's actually one of the reasons why armor as dice, while not really great for feeling well protected in the pre-V5 mechanics, actually makes sense on a level. It's never guaranteed to work perfectly in real combat conditions as opposed to what companies can do in a controlled setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The V5/damage-to-bashing rules are absolutely fine. </div> </div> </div>The concept by itself isn't bad. It's just how hitting a vampire in the head with an ax is mechanically the same whether or not the vampire is wearing a steal helmet that would keep the ax from delivering severe damage to their skull.<br /> <br /> For a comparison, VtR 2e has both armor (selectively) downgrading damage to bashing, and vampires treating all normal weapons as bashing instead of lethal, without making armor benefit-less to vampires, because armor can do more for you than downgrade damage types.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383753#post1383753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they? I always just assumed that breaking their bones caused them to move in a much more blatantly unnatural way, since they are corpses animated by magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>In every edition of VtM so far, including V5, vampires suffer penalties as they rack up damage. It would seem quite the oversight for five editions of VtM to skip the idea that vampires are supposed to be immune to penalties from having their bodies mangled and have things like frenzies explicitly ignore some of these complications, if that was the intent.<br /> <br /> In V5's advanced combat rules, a vampire is the example character for the Crippling Injuries option, so it would be very strange for them to not be capable of suffering those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383765#post1383765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is mechanically represented by the Critical Injury and the related penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't address the issue that the extra layer of protect armor provides does nothing to stop a crippling injury from happening to a vampire. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beyond that, verisimilitude can (and should) be sacrificed for mechanical balance. </div> </div> </div>Besides the rather... controversial nature of that assertion...<br /> <br /> What mechanical balance? Nobody's made a serious case that the way armor works in V5, and how that interacts with how vampires deal with physical damage in V5, is a significant issue of balance. Even more so, there's no case that there's no way to make a balanced armor rule that does go against verisimilitude so drastically.<br /> <br /> Ideally, we'd have a rule that does do justice to both verisimilitude and balance. It seems like V5 sacrifices both for the simplicity of armor's bonus be an automatic function.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383797#post1383797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;25794&quot;]Just taking a note that you may want to even it up a bit. Maybe a post about something other than negativity for every one that is.<br /> <br /> Just being helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not your role in the forums to tone-policy people, nor play mod when you feel like it. Esp. to just follow people you disagree with to do so without actually adding to the conversation; which could be seen as thread crapping and an actual rules violation.<br /> <br /> You're not being helpful, you're actively making the forums more heated. Stop it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T14:01:24-07:00","id":1383838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383835#post1383835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not your role in the forums to tone-policy people, nor play mod when you feel like it. Esp. to just follow people you disagree with to do so without actually adding to the conversation; which could be seen as thread crapping and an actual rules violation.<br /> <br /> You're not being helpful, you're actively making the forums more heated. Stop it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavy Arms....<br /> <br /> [beat]<br /> <br /> I *AM* a moderator. Look immediately to the left of this post under member.<br /> <br /> Never lecture another poster on what they are supposed to do again. Report them if you feel strongly they're breaking the rules. Consider that an official warning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B0