/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T17:18:23-07:00","id":1383873,"title":"","content":"Congrats CTPhipps, well deserved. Now back to the show. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T17:50:12-07:00","id":1383880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383859#post1383859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Prince made me an offer to betray the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> So I did.<br /> <br /> DUN DUN DUN</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Congrats. <br /> <br /> Enjoy your discussions. Best I see myself out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T05:18:14-07:00","id":1383943,"title":"","content":"I think there is practical merits to keeping armor a relatively weak stat. One, it keep elders scary, because if you, say, crash an armored van into her business luncheon, the Prince isn't significantly squishier because your coterie is armored up like the Micheline Man and she's wearing a tasteful dinner dress. Two, it preserves the movie flavor of vampires in general, because vampires don't run around in heavy armor in most movies/novels. Vampires generally dress in mundane, if gothically styled, clothing, or light leather armor. The typical movie/novel vampireverse is essentially a D&amp;D Rogueverse, where everyone is light and cunning and agile.<br /> <br /> In other words, armor is nerfed in this game for the same flavor reasons that the lighter armored classes in D&amp;D have excuses why they can't wear heavy armor. In the case of D&amp;D, it's generally because they can't use important class powers while wearing heavy armor. In Vampire, it's because armor itself is of limited value. Both are really just game mechanics designed to enforce a stylistic flavor via preventing the Rogues and Bards from plating up like Paladins and Fighters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T09:29:56-07:00","id":1383964,"title":"","content":"How many dracula films have given the man full-plate? DnD 5e has some wonderful 'vampire knight' variants. Having armour work as it's supposed to doesn't make elders less scary. If you crashed an elders place suited up whilst they were in their birthday suit, the elder is still scary, because they're too fast/don't even need the armour/escaped before you could even make a proper move/used supernatural charisma to have you turn your gun on your allies. And besides, the point of fearing mortals was that they could muster armour and big guns and so on, and young neonates had an edge in that they were familiar with things like 'truck bomb' and 'MG-42'. <br /> <br /> VTM isn't <i>Buffy the Vampire slayer </i> or <i>Grimm. </i><b>Hunting an elder is like a heist</b>, and are hiest films about careful planing and execution with carefully selected equipment and the vain hope that nothing will go wrong. Your average anarch looking to hunt an elder isn't donning his favourite trenchcoat and picking one of the many archaic novelty weapons in his closet so that he can have a fair fight with an elder; age VS the power of friendship, they're wondering how they can safely source that elusive MG-42/Truck bomb and how they can use them without incurring an overabundance of attention pre- or post- assassination attempt. Killing an elder isn't buffy and co patroling the streets for a baddy, it's an act of terrorism or organized crime where the police have a good chance of getting involved. At the very least, the body armour will be great for the masquerade once you visibly get shot eight times. You aren't leather dressed for a larp, you're dressed for highly illegal business. Vampire is a game of paranoia: You wear what increases your odds of success, not what passes for cool in young adult fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T09:49:30-07:00","id":1383968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383792#post1383792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a><br /> Getting disembowled is still inconvenient, even if you don't need those organs to live. Having your muscles shredded, losing limbs or your head. What's better than having 'superficial' damage? No damage at all!</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why we had soak rolls in previous editions.......for this very reason.....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T13:27:35-07:00","id":1384005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383943#post1383943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is practical merits to keeping armor a relatively weak stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be powerful as much as useful enough to avoid breaking immersion for people.<br /> <br /> Let's take vampires out of the combat for a second (because this applies to mortals too).<br /> <br /> You send your ghoul to go beat up some mortal with a baseball bat because for whatever reason that's deemed an effective tactic for this hypothetical. That mortal played football in college and happens to still have his protective gear. Realizing he has a few moments, the mortal tries to prepare for the fight as best he can.<br /> <br /> IRL, getting all that padding on is a no brainer if you have the time. You'd much rather have a football helmet on if someone's swinging a baseball bat at you, than take in on your unprotected skull.<br /> <br /> By the V5 rules, there's no difference. It's superficial damage either way, so mortals putting on protective gear in such situations has no point.<br /> <br /> To get more hyperbolic in terms of a situation, a mortal facing a mortal opponent in plate armor can deal damage almost as effectively with punches as they can with pistols... and the only difference there is the weapon damage bonus. Punching someone covered head to toe with steel is equally effective as punching someone wearing nothing.<br /> <br /> Pre-V5 armor was already weak. The dice bonus to soak was massively outmatched by what damage pools can get to in the game, and high soak armors meant big penalties to Dexterity rolls (aka the most important combat stat). Most vampires in Pre-V5 had minimal incentive to wear more than Class One armor (aka keeping the visual aesthetics of leather clad warriors) because the help from more soak was easily outweighed by the Dex penalties, and vampires already have good soak anyway (plus as noted, it helps with the Masquerade to have some armor on to excuse you taking a bunch of hits). But at least you could understand why vampires might wear armor, and certainly why squishy humans would wear armor by default in serious combat situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In other words, armor is nerfed in this game for the same flavor reasons that the lighter armored classes in D&amp;D have excuses why they can't wear heavy armor. In the case of D&amp;D, it's generally because they can't use important class powers while wearing heavy armor. In Vampire, it's because armor itself is of limited value. Both are really just game mechanics designed to enforce a stylistic flavor via preventing the Rogues and Bards from plating up like Paladins and Fighters. </div> </div> </div>There's two big problems with this.<br /> <br /> First, D&amp;D doesn't make armor useless by making it weak. It uses the same thing Pre-V5 VtM armor did to encourage these things: penalize important traits so some characters would avoid armor to avoid the penalties, and others wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Second, V5 is also going to set the mechanical tone for the rest of the games. Armor might not be a big deal for vampires, but it's a huge deal for some of their enemies (vampire hunters), and for games like Mage and CtD where characters don't have default supernaturally tough bodies. W5 is going to struggle with making effective First Teams if Pentex's hit squads can't use armor to equalize fights with Garou any more. Hitmarks are going to really struggle to pull their Terminator-but-for-mages tricks if all that internal armor they have is pointless. Etc.<br /> <br /> V5's rules aren't just preventing rogues and bards from plating up like paladins and fighters... it's preventing paladins and fighters from having the benefits from armor they'd want for giving up on the perks the others get by not wearing so much armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T18:12:35-07:00","id":1384065,"title":"","content":"V5 isn\u2019t D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> In the modern era, the population at large generally doesn\u2019t wear personal armour. Vampires in the setting are mostly attempting to live a clandestine life hidden amongst urban, civilized populations - in the modern era - and are not going to want to draw attention to themselves by walking around in full plate armour.<br /> <br /> The rules for armour in V5, therefore, are aimed at those people who are likely to wear it - special services, swat teams etc. In these cases, as with real life, what body armour does is convert what would be lethal damage to the body into non lethal damage. That is what the rules do. However, seeing as most lethal damage is already converted to non-lethal damage for vampires as it is - because they are magical, undead beings - the impact of wearing such armour is negligible.<br /> <br /> Now this is the rules as they are. They are functional and logical in their conclusion. If you want to develop rules to allow armour to function in a manner that would be comparable to D&amp;D, you may need to develop ideas further or in a different way. Good luck with that. However, V5 isn\u2019t D&amp;D. Never has been; never will be. Nor are the other WoD lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-26-2020, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T19:04:15-07:00","id":1384070,"title":"","content":"Vampires and archaic armor does not equal D&amp;D. It equals Vampire: the Dark Ages, which is a 24-year established historical setting for the game. If that becomes mechanically nonfunctional due to Murphy's Rules involving period arms and armor, that means that everyone will have an additional reason to play using V20A DA instead of V5 when the latter gets around to attempting historical settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T19:18:36-07:00","id":1384071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384070#post1384070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires and archaic armor does not equal D&amp;D. It equals Vampire: the Dark Ages, which is a 24-year established historical setting for the game. If that becomes mechanically nonfunctional due to Murphy's Rules involving period arms and armor, that means that everyone will have an additional reason to play using V20A DA instead of V5 when the latter gets around to attempting historical settings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, some other posters here were making comparisons to D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> V5 as it stands in the corebook, isn\u2019t Vampire: The Dark Ages either. The game, in the standalone core rules, is specifically designed for modern era play. It may be the case that other eras will be looked at in supplements - maybe it is something to suggest for The Player\u2019s Guide - but they can address historically niche armour rules in those supplements when they get round to it. People can surely play Vampire: The Dark Ages in the meantime if they want, but this has no bearing on where V5 rules are at currently if they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T19:28:13-07:00","id":1384074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384071#post1384071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, some other posters here were making comparisons to D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> V5 as it stands in the corebook, isn\u2019t Vampire: The Dark Ages either. The game, in the standalone core rules, is specifically designed for modern era play. It may be the case that other eras will be looked at in supplements - maybe it is something to suggest for The Player\u2019s Guide - but they can address historically niche armour rules in those supplements when they get round to it. People can surely play Vampire: The Dark Ages in the meantime if they want, but this has no bearing on where V5 rules are at currently if they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The effects of armor don't really seem like something that should be optional rules for historical supplements. To add yet more sticks onto the fire, Changeling loves its pseudo-medieval aesthetics, and wraiths will often have very eclectic equipment based on whatever they could scrounge up from the literal dust bins of history. These things need to be addressed well without having hot patches in books that people might not ever bother reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T19:41:16-07:00","id":1384078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384074#post1384074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The effects of armor don't really seem like something that should be optional rules for historical supplements. To add yet more sticks onto the fire, Changeling loves its pseudo-medieval aesthetics, and wraiths will often have very eclectic equipment based on whatever they could scrounge up from the literal dust bins of history. These things need to be addressed well without having hot patches in books that people might not ever bother reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Firstly because Storyteller has lots of examples of discrete rules used for different settings already. In the Wraith supplement for The Great War, for example, they introduce new combat initiative rules to simulate wartime battles. There isn\u2019t a necessity for every game to be using the same universal rules in every single aspect of play, and V5 doesn\u2019t have to be designed to incorporate every historical era or spinoff game within the pages of the core book alone. Its like arguing we need to have rules for space combat.<br /> <br /> Secondly, without being an expert on historical armour, I\u2019m pretty certain that the nature of combat has changed from the medieval era to the modern era, to the extent that modern body armour used by practitioners today has a different functional use to that used in previous eras. Moreover, while this could all present an interesting exercise in simulation, to debate the physics of how armour in different eras would work, again, this is hardly within the remit of the core rules of a game that explicitly is designed for the modern era alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-26-2020, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T19:57:40-07:00","id":1384081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384078#post1384078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. Firstly because Storyteller has lots of examples of discrete rules used for different settings already. In the Wraith supplement for The Great War, for example, they introduce new combat initiative rules to simulate wartime battles. There isn\u2019t a necessity for every game to be using the same universal rules in every single aspect of play, and V5 doesn\u2019t have to be designed to incorporate every historical era or spinoff game within the pages of the core book alone. Its like arguing we need to have rules for space combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might have flown a bit more easily if WW weren't hellbent on pushing that &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; thing and going crossover happy. As for space combat, it's way easier to pull a knife or machete on someone than it is to hitch a ride on a shuttle, and the setting as a whole doesn't have interstellar warships, so it doesn't enter into the conversation as a meaningful point of comparison, whereas the Neptunic anti-bite suit has given chain mesh a new use and might even buy you some time against a wereshark or other werebeast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Secondly, without being an expert on historical armour, I\u2019m pretty certain that the nature of combat has changed from the medieval era to the modern era, to the extent that modern body armour used by practitioners today has a different functional use to that used in previous eras. Moreover, while this could all present an interesting exercise in simulation, to debate the physics of how armour in different eras would work, again, this is hardly within the remit of the core rules of a game that explicitly is designed for the modern era alone. </div> </div> </div>It's in some types of armor not providing an effect against some effects. Kevlar won't stop a knife, but an anti-stab vest will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T20:16:44-07:00","id":1384086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384081#post1384081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might have flown a bit more easily if WW weren't hellbent on pushing that &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; thing and going crossover happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has absolutely nothing to do with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for space combat, it's way easier to pull a knife or machete on someone than it is to hitch a ride on a shuttle, and the setting as a whole doesn't have interstellar warships, so it doesn't enter into the conversation as a meaningful point of comparison, whereas the Neptunic anti-bite suit has given chain mesh a new use and might even buy you some time against a wereshark or other werebeast. </div> </div> </div>And by the same token, the game presented in the core rules doesn\u2019t need detailed rules for medieval style combat in it. It is set in the modern era. There are no rules for weresharks in the core rules either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's in some types of armor not providing an effect against some effects. Kevlar won't stop a knife, but an anti-stab vest will. </div> </div> </div>There isn\u2019t any pressing need for V5 to need to go into this detail for specific armour designs, any more than providing a break down of rules determining which specific type of car they should be driving. It is not the focus of the game and, again, never has been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T20:33:59-07:00","id":1384090,"title":"","content":"In addition to things like a Kevlar vest vs. a stab vest regarding how they'll perform there's a wider issue.<br /> <br /> A lot of people defending the V5 rules seem to be operating from the stance that modern armor works by &quot;transforming&quot; &quot;lethal&quot; attacks into non-lethal attacks. That an attack with a gun against bullet resistant armor changes something about the bullet so that it causes bruises instead of holes.<br /> <br /> The problem is that this is accomplishing by having the armor absorb as much of the force of the impact as possible, and thus transferring as little of the force to the armor wearer as possible.<br /> <br /> If you get shot while wearing Kevlar and get a cracked rib instead of a bullet passing through you, it's because all the energy necessary to push a bullet through your body was imparted into your vest instead of you.<br /> <br /> That's where the V5 method falls down. This is actually something that hasn't changed in thousands of years. The technology has gotten better. Hard vs. soft vs. hybrid armors have come in and out of fashion in reaction to weapon technology improving. But the job of all armor is to absorb the energy instead of letting it through. The reason a war hammer striking plate mail causes a concussion instead of a lethal skull fracture is the same reason a 9mm pistol shot into Kevlar causes a massive bruise instead of a punctured liver: the armors absorb the damage so the target doesn't have to absorb as much of it.<br /> <br /> There's no logical reason why a bullet that hits a Kevlar vest worn by a vampire does the same amount of damage as to a vampire that doesn't wear armor, because the Kevlar vest wearing vampire literally has less damaging energy for their body to absorb.<br /> <br /> Or to put this a different way, if you accept that a ,22 pistol does less damage to vampires than a .357 magnum pistol, as the V5 rules say they do, you cannot adequately explain why without showing the V5 armor rules don't make sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T20:44:45-07:00","id":1384093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384090#post1384090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no logical reason why a bullet that hits a Kevlar vest worn by a vampire does the same amount of damage as to a vampire that doesn't wear armor, because the Kevlar vest wearing vampire literally has less damaging energy for their body to absorb.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is. Vampires are magical beings that don\u2019t suffer lethal damage from things like bullets. Having a Kevlar vest that stops damaging energy is irrelevant to them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, can we talk about how the combat rules in V20 are entirely dysfunctional now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-26-2020, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T21:10:16-07:00","id":1384098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1383765#post1383765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normal humans power through a lot of injuries that should keep them down in stress and anger. The Beast is just doing the same thing on a more monstrous scale. It's not an unrealistic concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I've read an account of a soldier being caught in a grenade blast and running away upright for a few moments despite the bones of one leg turning out to have been shattered; and seen one of a hiker who threw off a half ton slab of rock that fell on him to prevent it from crushing him, even through the effort ripped all kinds of shoulder and back muscles loose. It's amazing what you can do when your body's entire supply of adrenaline gets dumped into your bloodstream at once and you're not being hampered by any pain feedback from overloading your muscles and joints.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T23:17:56-07:00","id":1384109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384086#post1384086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has absolutely nothing to do with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be so sure about that. There isn't nearly as much of the deniability as past editions, what with an identified Fenrir showing up in an introductory adventure where the players might not have any idea of what that means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And by the same token, the game presented in the core rules doesn\u2019t need detailed rules for medieval style combat in it. It is set in the modern era. </div> </div> </div>The modern era where you can still shank someone with a shiv more readily than shoot them, yes. And then there's the matter of staking. Forget the medieval armor; close quarters combat is still very much a thing, and there are modern armor types that can make a difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are no rules for weresharks in the core rules either. </div> </div> </div>No, but there are plenty of other bitey things that could conceivably hurt Kindred very badly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There isn\u2019t any pressing need for V5 to need to go into this detail for specific armour designs, any more than providing a break down of rules determining which specific type of car they should be driving. It is not the focus of the game and, again, never has been. </div> </div> </div>We're not talking about detailed, specific armor designs, but very broad armor concept types. And, in this context, it absolutely makes sense to add a stab/shot column with yes, no, and half as designations for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T23:28:35-07:00","id":1384111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384109#post1384109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't be so sure about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sure about it. It\u2019s nonsense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The modern era where you can still shank someone with a shiv more readily than shoot them, yes. And then there's the matter of staking. Forget the medieval armor; close quarters combat is still very much a thing, and there are modern armor types that can make a difference.<br /> <br /> No, but there are plenty of other bitey things that could conceivably hurt Kindred very badly.<br /> <br /> We're not talking about detailed, specific armor designs, but very broad armor concept types. And, in this context, it absolutely makes sense to add a stab/shot column with yes, no, and half as designations for it. </div> </div> </div>All of this is just spurious. There is nothing stopping you from developing whatever rules you want for contrived play, but the reality is that the amour rules presented in V5 are perfectly serviceable for the genre and setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T01:34:09-07:00","id":1384125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384093#post1384093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is. Vampires are magical beings that don\u2019t suffer lethal damage from things like bullets. Having a Kevlar vest that stops damaging energy is irrelevant to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they do suffer damage from bullets. the entirety of your argument has been upended by simple attention to facts. Vampires suffer damage from bullets, ergo, when expecting to be shot at, armour is a good idea, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T01:59:45-07:00","id":1384127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384125#post1384125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they do suffer damage from bullets. the entirety of your argument has been upended by simple attention to facts. Vampires suffer damage from bullets, ergo, when expecting to be shot at, armour is a good idea, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>They suffer bashing damage from bullets, which is what the armour reduces the damage to - thus being redundant. This being the entirety of your pedantic argument reduced accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-27-2020, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T02:01:43-07:00","id":1384128,"title":"","content":"Well, I feel the armor rules were badly handled in V5. Some people agree, some don't. For those who don't, maybe we can just posit a simple hack optional rule that will help and maybe make a bit of noise somehow to request it be placed as an optional rule in a future V5 vampire book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T02:29:57-07:00","id":1384133,"title":"","content":"Maybe: light armor turns aggravated damage to superficial damage, medium armor does this and reduces damage by 1, and heavy armor does this and reduces armor by 3. Armor usually does not protect against things like Fire and falling damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T02:39:11-07:00","id":1384134,"title":"","content":"Well, the simplest without redoing any numbers would be something like:<br /> <br /> If an attack would already do all superficial damage, armor reduces the total damage take by half its rating before the superficial damage itself is halved. So if your vampire is wearing Kevlar, and is shot for 6 superficial damage, it's reduced to 4 (Kevlar has an armor rating of 4, divide by 2 to get 2, and 6 - 2 = 4), and then halved because it's superficial damage to 2 final damage recorded.<br /> <br /> It's a bit clunky, but the armor ratings are too high to reduce their full value, or reduce after normal superficial halving.<br /> <br /> Something that should work on top of that without having to change the math (so, again, something that might be added into a supplement since it doesn't mean just starting over completely):<br /> <br /> All armors have three ratings General/Firearms/Special. General applies to hand-to-hand combat, thrown non-explosive weapons, bow based weapons and the like. Firearms applies to guns and some other modern weapons if those weapons specify. Special is for protection against non-standard damaging effects such as a fire-fighter's gear helping them fend off fire, or a gas mask protecting you from pepper spray (bit of a guess as chemical weapons aren't really covered). If the total of all three is greater than 6, and for each 6 rating, the armor imparts a cumulative -1 penalty to Dexterity rolls.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T03:42:55-07:00","id":1384146,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My personal tweak to the V5 armor rules:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Change the text on page 304 to:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> Armor</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Each point of armor changes 1 point of Aggravated damage from puncturing or bladed weapons (per damage roll) to Superficial damage, which is then halved as usual. If the armor value exeeds the amount of sustained superficial damage, reduce the final amount of damage by 1 to a minimum of 0. While this protection is in general more useful to mortals and thin-bloods, as vampires already consider those types of damage Superficial, even vampires profit from being prepared.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wearing heavier armor just hightens the chance to get that extra damage reduction of -1 and doesn't take all the spotlight from Toughness (Fortitude 2).</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T04:49:35-07:00","id":1384165,"title":"","content":"Maybe each point of armor changes 1 point of aggravated damage to superficial damage and when there is no more aggravated damage every remaining 2 points reduce superficial damage by 1 (min 0), after which damage is halved, rounded down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T07:24:51-07:00","id":1384187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384127#post1384127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They suffer bashing damage from bullets, which is what the armour reduces the damage to - thus being redundant. This being the entirety of your pedantic argument reduced accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Went straight over your head I see. You're looking at mechanics and saying 'Hah, of course armour is useless, just look at these mechanics' Whilst I'm looking at everything and noting that 'The mechanics are not at all in line with reality'. I don't get how we're looking at the issue of 'Getting hacked at with or without armour is the same thing for a vampire because that's how the mechanics work' and coming to different conclusions; I think it's terrible and you apparently think it's fantastic. Are these your genuine thoughts or is your bias riding you through these fields?<br /> <br /> Giving a vampire armour should be like giving an ogre an iron club. The way vampire physiology works, it's supremely beneficial. Making armour literally innefective based on the fact that a vampire wears it is silly. What are the weaknesses of vampires now? Fire,faith,sunlight, the inability to gain advantages from wearing steel on their person... It's ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T08:37:38-07:00","id":1384194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384111#post1384111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of this is just spurious. There is nothing stopping you from developing whatever rules you want for contrived play, but the reality is that the amour rules presented in V5 are perfectly serviceable for the genre and setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no it doesn't. The complete opposite of that in fact<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384065#post1384065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 isn\u2019t D&amp;]<br /> <br /> Now this is the rules as they are. They are functional and logical in their conclusion. If you want to develop rules to allow armour to function in a manner that would be comparable to D&amp;D, you may need to develop ideas further or in a different way. Good luck with that. However, V5 isn\u2019t D&amp;D. Never has been; never will be. Nor are the other WoD lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, they are, like V5 in general, nonfunctional and illogical. V20 had issues, but at least it had a combats system, V5 has a radioactive dumpster fire filled with used nappies claiming to be a combat system","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-27-2020, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T09:28:07-07:00","id":1384202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pangur B\u00e1n</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384146#post1384146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My personal tweak to the V5 armor rules:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Change the text on page 304 to:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br /> Armor</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Each point of armor changes 1 point of Aggravated damage from puncturing or bladed weapons (per damage roll) to Superficial damage, which is then halved as usual. If the armor value exeeds the amount of sustained superficial damage, reduce the final amount of damage by 1 to a minimum of 0. While this protection is in general more useful to mortals and thin-bloods, as vampires already consider those types of damage Superficial, even vampires profit from being prepared.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#454545\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wearing heavier armor just hightens the chance to get that extra damage reduction of -1 and doesn't take all the spotlight from Toughness (Fortitude 2).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384133#post1384133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe: light armor turns aggravated damage to superficial damage, medium armor does this and reduces damage by 1, and heavy armor does this and reduces armor by 3. Armor usually does not protect against things like Fire and falling damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Armor becomes BETTER than Fortitude and any other damage reducing power in the game except for Flesh of Marble, as the game's design generally has a minimum of 1 damage on reductions. V5's mechanical design does not function in a way that having armor reduce damage stays balanced within the system as designed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T09:51:22-07:00","id":1384207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384202#post1384202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Armor becomes BETTER than Fortitude and any other damage reducing power in the game except for Flesh of Marble, as the game's design generally has a minimum of 1 damage on reductions. V5's mechanical design does not function in a way that having armor reduce damage stays balanced within the system as designed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, like a Raufoss-Round is BETTER than Lethal Body (Potence 1) and Fist of Caine (Potence 5) (not using a rouse check for Fist of Caine, ignoring up to 6 armor instead of 5 and being applicable from a distance). Since armor does not need to replace Toughness (Fortitude 2) but works together with it, I do not see the problem there. You could argue, that using weapons and armor would just hand characters tools, that others need disciplines for. Then again, nobody will disarm your fists or look weird at you for wearing a kevlar vest in a private night club. Reducing damage by 1 when wearing massive armor does not unbalance the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","user":"Pangur B\u00e1n","date":". 04-27-2020, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T10:00:29-07:00","id":1384210,"title":"","content":"(Snipp) not worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 04-27-2020, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T11:25:00-07:00","id":1384228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384194#post1384194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, they are, like V5 in general, nonfunctional and illogical. V20 had issues, but at least it had a combats system, V5 has a radioactive dumpster fire filled with used nappies claiming to be a combat system</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome to dislike V5 and healthy discussion is based around preferences but could we dial down the hyperbole?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\"> Forum Rules - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Onyx Path provides this forum as a gathering place for players and readers of our games. We want the forums to be a welcoming place for as many folks as possible. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Rule 3#<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T12:22:22-07:00","id":1384238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384187#post1384187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Went straight over your head I see. You're looking at mechanics and saying 'Hah, of course armour is useless, just look at these mechanics' Whilst I'm looking at everything and noting that 'The mechanics are not at all in line with reality'. I don't get how we're looking at the issue of 'Getting hacked at with or without armour is the same thing for a vampire because that's how the mechanics work' and coming to different conclusions; I think it's terrible and you apparently think it's fantastic. Are these your genuine thoughts or is your bias riding you through these fields?<br /> <br /> Giving a vampire armour should be like giving an ogre an iron club. The way vampire physiology works, it's supremely beneficial. Making armour literally innefective based on the fact that a vampire wears it is silly. What are the weaknesses of vampires now? Fire,faith,sunlight, the inability to gain advantages from wearing steel on their person... It's ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>What went went over your head, when reading these rules, is that the writers and most players of the game regard these rules as perfectly good. This is because the idea of 'vampire armour' against weapons in which they do not regard as a lethal threat is not ever going to be a priority. The mechanics are in line with a reality whereby magical beings exist, and you are playing them. This means that the rules of physics, of which I do not regard yourself as being an expert on, is not something that the rules of the game need to dwell on. &quot;Vampire armour\u201d is not even a thing, and vampire physiology is entirely fictional, so to start making a claim that you know how vampire physiology works is your own delusion, and ridiculous in and of itself.<br /> <br /> One might very well ask you whether these are &quot;your genuine thoughts or is your bias riding you through these fields?&quot; because every other post you have ever made on this site has been designed to attack V5 - this line of attack is no different. It also ignores the broader point that the previous versions of Vampire combat were so entirely dysfunctional that to bring up this solitary issue in V5, which is a non issue for me, clearly shows your bias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-27-2020, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T12:41:44-07:00","id":1384244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384202#post1384202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5's mechanical design does not function in a way that having armor reduce damage stays balanced within the system as designed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is... more damning of the system than defending it if you really think about it.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I agree with the sentiment at all. V5 can handle equipment adding to damage... so it seems fairly simple for it to handle equipment subtracting from damage. If it really can't... that's fairly large design flaw.<br /> <br /> I agree that however unrealistic mundane armor shouldn't be allowed to negate an attack's damage completely (that way lies endless combat of armored tanks never hurting each other, and it goes against the grain that a successful roll should have an effect) or at least should only happen in extreme situations, but the idea that armor can't be modeled as limited damage reduction seems extremely off to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T12:49:07-07:00","id":1384248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384194#post1384194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, they are, like V5 in general, nonfunctional and illogical. V20 had issues, but at least it had a combats system, V5 has a radioactive dumpster fire filled with used nappies claiming to be a combat system</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 (and previous editions) had a dysfunctional combat system which attempted to square-peg the dice pool system used in the rest of the game into a three-tier Initiative-Attack-Damage process, used in other games, with competed rolls in each stage.<br /> <br /> Originally, or at least formally from V2 onwards, Initiative was also based on dicepool rolling, but this was abandoned from VRev onwards because of the tendency of too many rolls ending up with the same outcome. If all the characters roll the same number of success it failed to differentiate an initiative order - and so made all the dice rolling redundant. So they replaced it with a D&amp;D style, roll of a single die and add a trait-based bonus. V5 cuts all this out by making Initiative a narrative process for the most part - people mostly resolve their conflicts in an order that suits the narrative or simply check comparative scores in relevant traits if needed, without the need for an additional dice roll. In practice, what this means is that the narrative of the combat is prevalent, rather than just a randomized affair requiring a degree of book-keeping.<br /> <br /> The Attack roll in V20 was a contested roll, which matches the rest of the game system, but unlike the rest of the system, you also had to follow on with a contested damage roll, which incorporated an armour rating into Soak as the opposing roll. What this meant in effect is that there was more randomness in the system than in other parts of the game. Even rolling five successes on an attack, which would be outstanding in any other roll, would not necessarily lead to any effect at all once other rolls were added on. The same is true of the defensive rolls. What this meant was that neither the trait values of the participants, nor the armour value were actually reliable in practice. You could have the best, toughest armour that anybody could imagine, but if your rolls were randomly bad they\u2019d have no effect.<br /> <br /> This doesn\u2019t reflect reality - indeed, the major point of note with a modern kevlar vest is that it does reliably stop lethal damage from certain attacks. So, if we are going to criticize V5 armour rules, one should take into account that previously used rules weren\u2019t that good or effective either.<br /> <br /> In V5, what armour does is reliably consistent in the rules, but its effects for vampires are negligible because of their magical situation - which is, most lethal attacks that it prevents are not lethal for them anyway. Smart, neat rules which put the emphasis on the narrative. Modern vampires in modern nights don\u2019t generally have a need to walk around in heavy armour which pretty much matches any type of vampire fiction in any other medium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-27-2020, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T13:21:18-07:00","id":1384251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384244#post1384244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that however unrealistic mundane armor shouldn't be allowed to negate an attack's damage completely (that way lies endless combat of armored tanks never hurting each other, and it goes against the grain that a successful roll should have an effect) or at least should only happen in extreme situations, but the idea that armor can't be modeled as limited damage reduction seems extremely off to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>But are there not multiple rules to prevent exactly that and other rules to allow for exactly that?<br /> Preventing: There is the rule of Three Turns and Out, preventing endless combat, unless one is actively aiming for that.<br /> Preventing: Toughness (Fortitude 2) has a minimum of 1 damage.<br /> Enabling: Vampires mend damage with a rouse check reducing damage by at least one.<br /> Enabling: Flesh of Marble (Fortitude 5) ignores the first or greatest source of damage per turn completely.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, reducing the damage sustained by one, if the armor value the vampire wears is greater than the original damage value does not unbalance the game and does not lead to endless combat but provides all vampires, including those with Fortitude, some use of wearing armor, just like basically all vampires would profit from using a weapon (except maybe for Fist of Caine when specifically fighting against other vampires in close combat).<br /> <br /> But of course: I'm not married to some kind of design philosophy and just try to provide a rules tweak for players and storytellers that are unhappy with the V5 armor rules and every table has its own rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T13:30:14-07:00","id":1384254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384248#post1384248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V20 (and previous editions) had a dysfunctional combat system which attempted to square-peg the dice pool system used in the rest of the game into a three-tier Initiative-Attack-Damage process, used in other games, with competed rolls in each stage.<br /> <br /> Originally, or at least formally from V2 onwards, Initiative was also based on dicepool rolling, but this was abandoned from VRev onwards because of the tendency of too many rolls ending up with the same outcome. If all the characters roll the same number of success it failed to differentiate an initiative order - and so made all the dice rolling redundant. So they replaced it with a D&amp;D style, roll of a single die and add a trait-based bonus. V5 cuts all this out by making Initiative a narrative process for the most part - people mostly resolve their conflicts in an order that suits the narrative or simply check comparative scores in relevant traits if needed, without the need for an additional dice roll. In practice, what this means is that the narrative of the combat is prevalent, rather than just a randomized affair requiring a degree of book-keeping.<br /> <br /> The Attack roll in V20 was a contested roll, which matches the rest of the game system, but unlike the rest of the system, you also had to follow on with a contested damage roll, which incorporated an armour rating into Soak as the opposing roll. What this meant in effect is that there was more randomness in the system than in other parts of the game. Even rolling five successes on an attack, which would be outstanding in any other roll, would not necessarily lead to any effect at all once other rolls were added on. The same is true of the defensive rolls. What this meant was that neither the trait values of the participants, nor the armour value were actually reliable in practice. You could have the best, toughest armour that anybody could imagine, but if your rolls were randomly bad they\u2019d have no effect.<br /> <br /> This doesn\u2019t reflect reality - indeed, the major point of note with a modern kevlar vest is that it does reliably stop lethal damage from certain attacks. So, if we are going to criticize V5 armour rules, one should take into account that previously used rules weren\u2019t that good or effective either.<br /> <br /> In V5, what armour does is reliably consistent in the rules, but its effects for vampires are negligible because of their magical situation - which is, most lethal attacks that it prevents are not lethal for them anyway. Smart, neat rules which put the emphasis on the narrative. Modern vampires in modern nights don\u2019t generally have a need to walk around in heavy armour which pretty much matches any type of vampire fiction in any other medium.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vastly prefer V20s way of doing combat, and Vampires in body armour fits with some more modern portrayals (Blade for instance, or Bram Stoker's Dracula, the movie with a plate armoured Vlad Tepes) it also fits with suspension of disbelief, a creature that can be pierced with a stake can be pierced by arrows, bullets, buckshot etc, they may care less, or with the right discipline not care at all, but when expecting heavy combat, armour works. <br /> <br /> Vampires should not fear gang bangers with pistols, to hey should fear SWAT or SPECOPS, <br /> <br /> Given how shallow and hollow V5 conflict in general is, it's not fun, and I don't care what happens to characters in that system, the skeleton to hang the story on is missing almost entirely, so the story collapses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T13:31:29-07:00","id":1384255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384228#post1384228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're welcome to dislike V5 and healthy discussion is based around preferences but could we dial down the hyperbole?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/o...06-forum-rules</a><br /> <br /> Rule 3#</div> </div> </div> </div>That was as polite as I can be about this...thing.... If I am being more honest the entire game line feels like the developers screaming insults into the face of the fan base while crapping on VtM","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T13:59:57-07:00","id":1384258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pangur B\u00e1n</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384251#post1384251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But are there not multiple rules to prevent exactly that and other rules to allow for exactly that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I did specify &quot;mundane&quot; there. Disciplines are meant to do what the mundane cannot.<br /> <br /> As for the Three Turns rule, it might stop you from continuing a tank-off, but the mechanical resolution issue of neither side gaining an advantage remains if armor damage reduction is too strong.<br /> <br /> Also, I do agree that V5 can handle some damage reduction via armor... my suggested rule actually goes farther with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T14:03:19-07:00","id":1384259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384254#post1384254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I vastly prefer V20s way of doing combat, and Vampires in body armour fits with some more modern portrayals (Blade for instance, or Bram Stoker's Dracula, the movie with a plate armoured Vlad Tepes) it also fits with suspension of disbelief, a creature that can be pierced with a stake can be pierced by arrows, bullets, buckshot etc, they may care less, or with the right discipline not care at all, but when expecting heavy combat, armour works.<br /> <br /> Vampires should not fear gang bangers with pistols, to hey should fear SWAT or SPECOPS,<br /> <br /> Given how shallow and hollow V5 conflict in general is, it's not fun, and I don't care what happens to characters in that system, the skeleton to hang the story on is missing almost entirely, so the story collapses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everybody is entitled to their choice, but there is nothing in the V20 rules that fit better with modern portrayals.<br /> <br /> Blade is a s sort of half-vampire - probably more akin to a Thin-Blood who would make some use out of body armour in V5 as they don\u2019t have the resistances that full vampires do. I\u2019d note that at least V5 has rules incorporated for playing Thin-Bloods if you like Blade-like characters. Bram Stoker\u2019s Dracula (as in the movie) didn\u2019t walk around Victorian London wearing armour and didn\u2019t get portrayed in modern 21st century nights at all - in fact, the only time he did wear armor was before he was a vampire, during the medieval period - so your examples aren\u2019t great. I can\u2019t see how having randomized soaking is a better simulation of how armour is supposed to work in any circumstance.<br /> <br /> V5 combat isn\u2019t shallow or hollow. It works in a dramatic and fun way, where story is emphasized over meaningless dice rolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-27-2020, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T14:04:11-07:00","id":1384260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384255#post1384255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was as polite as I can be about this...thing.... If I am being more honest the entire game line feels like the developers screaming insults into the face of the fan base while crapping on VtM</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the developers were\u2019t doing that, which is why its hyperbole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T14:15:21-07:00","id":1384263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384111#post1384111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sure about it. It\u2019s nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to be awfully surprised when crossover dumps something strange on you, then, rather than working through the system issues before hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of this is just spurious. There is nothing stopping you from developing whatever rules you want for contrived play, but the reality is that the amour rules presented in V5 are perfectly serviceable for the genre and setting. </div> </div> </div>Ghoul animals have been a thing since forever, werewolves are apparently even more eager to bag Kindred for hash marks, and it's trivially easy for vampire hunters to put shotgun shells on sticks and use them to ward off vampire attacks, to say nothing of the more old-fashioned, sword-wielding Church types with faith. All of these are bog-standard threats that show up to menace the nightly existence of Kindred, offering no quarter and not being inclined to talk. There is nothing contrived at all about them showing up and ruining the night; they are genre conventions all unto their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T14:16:46-07:00","id":1384264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384255#post1384255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was as polite as I can be about this...thing.... If I am being more honest the entire game line feels like the developers screaming insults into the face of the fan base while crapping on VtM</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, probably something you may have to keep to PMs then. Edition Wars are a thing people can no longer engage in. It is the end of an era.<br /> <br /> Even if nothing prevents you from saying you don't like it and think V20 is far superior.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T14:24:53-07:00","id":1384266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384263#post1384263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're going to be awfully surprised when crossover dumps something strange on you, then, rather than working through the system issues before hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won\u2019t be because the Werewolf developers have already pointed out that while some rules will be consistent with V5, other rules will be bespoke to how Werewolf is meant to work. Moreover, the marketing tag of 'One World of Darkness\u2019 that you cited, literally has nothing to do, whatsoever, with the intricate discussion of how armour is supposed to work in the game. It is a nonsense claim to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ghoul animals have been a thing since forever, werewolves are apparently even more eager to bag Kindred for hash marks, and it's trivially easy for vampire hunters to put shotgun shells on sticks and use them to ward off vampire attacks, to say nothing of the more old-fashioned, sword-wielding Church types with faith. All of these are bog-standard threats that show up to menace the nightly existence of Kindred, offering no quarter and not being inclined to talk. There is nothing contrived at all about them showing up and ruining the night; they are genre conventions all unto their own. </div> </div> </div>None of this actually co