y/etc. do for the WoD games.<br /> <br /> Until something changes, we're not getting any new forums or sub-forums added to the boards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T16:57:15-07:00","id":1384299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384297#post1384297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As has been explained in the Trouble Tickets forum, the forum software is heavily broken in many behind-the-scenes functions. The only way to fix it would be a hard reset, and the frustration with it as, so far, not been sufficient to max the headache of a hard reset worth it.<br /> <br /> Whole new games like Dystopian Rising: Evolution, and new lines like Deviant for the CofD aren't getting their own forums and have to share, general forums like Demon/Hunter/Mummy/etc. do for the WoD games.<br /> <br /> Until something changes, we're not getting any new forums or sub-forums added to the boards.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a more simpler tone, it's also not that difficult to just respect where other posters disagree with you.<br /> <br /> It's not THAT hard to avoid threadcrapping.<br /> <br /> We're all vampire fans here, no matter the edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T17:03:30-07:00","id":1384300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384266#post1384266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won\u2019t be because the Werewolf developers have already pointed out that while some rules will be consistent with V5, other rules will be bespoke to how Werewolf is meant to work. Moreover, the marketing tag of 'One World of Darkness\u2019 that you cited, literally has nothing to do, whatsoever, with the intricate discussion of how armour is supposed to work in the game. It is a nonsense claim to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, it's more of the later games' problem of early Vampire problems dragging down the other lines with general rules that take a decade to revise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of this actually counters the point I made in any way. </div> </div> </div>What point did you make?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you originally cited Weresharks. </div> </div> </div>Ghoul animals would have been better as a more commonplace occurrence for V:tM, I suppose. In the end, it doesn't matter; melee combat is stuck to Vampire whether you happen to approve of its presence or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T17:04:52-07:00","id":1384301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384286#post1384286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe make a different board for V5 or V20 and before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think its a practical solution to the problem, largely because it underlines a division in the community which I think would be even more counterproductive in the long term. There is a mechanism that already exists where people can post a thread highlighting in brackets that it is [V20] or [V5] or any other edition. You could also use the typical notation of a \u2018+\u2019 to indicate positive comments only. However, beyond anything else, people just need to get along better.<br /> <br /> Maybe we could start the process right now - where everybody who has participated in this thread starts a new thread about any edition they like, discussing something positive about the game and including a \u2018+\u2019 sign in it. Would that be a challenge for everybody? We could actually have a bunch of new threads, which others can positively participate in as they like, and it might change the tone accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-27-2020, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T17:12:54-07:00","id":1384302,"title":"","content":"Understanding people like different editions for different reasons and that's okay is a hard long road.<br /> <br /> But probably the best road forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-27-2020, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T17:21:28-07:00","id":1384305,"title":"","content":"So... back to armor...<br /> <br /> A few house rules ideas were presented, it might be nice if some people with significant play experience with the game could give some feedback on them even if they aren't interested in using them? Is there some rule missed that specifically interacts messily with them? <br /> <br /> Mine was based on the idea that armor is rated 0/2/4/6 in V5. Do any of the supplement have armor rated as an odd number? Over six in a fashion that might imply a Dexterity penalty scheme? Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T17:43:22-07:00","id":1384309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384300#post1384300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case, it's more of the later games' problem of early Vampire problems dragging down the other lines with general rules that take a decade to revise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think there are many problems in the game that can\u2019t be fixed. I don\u2019t have any reason to believe that the developers do either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What point did you make? </div> </div> </div>That there is nothing stopping you from developing rules you want, but that the rules as written for V5 are perfectly serviceable for its genre and setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 'Ghoul animals would have been better as a more commonplace occurrence for V:tM, I suppose. In the end, it doesn't matter; melee combat is stuck to Vampire whether you happen to approve of its presence or not. </div> </div> </div> Fighting against ghoul animals or anything else, is not just a matter of wearing armour. Indeed, in the case of many encounters that could possibly happen in Vampire, it is often irrelevant because of the magical nature of the opponents and the general point that the game doesn\u2019t usually amount to a fantasy style crawl through different encounters. When violence occurs, in my games at least, it usually does so asa surprise attack or after a suspenseful build up. This does not usually give vampires time to stock up on armour that is quite unusual to own in modern society, and not typical of the vampires\u2019 usual garb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T17:51:07-07:00","id":1384310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384305#post1384305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... back to armor...<br /> <br /> A few house rules ideas were presented, it might be nice if some people with significant play experience with the game could give some feedback on them even if they aren't interested in using them? Is there some rule missed that specifically interacts messily with them?<br /> <br /> Mine was based on the idea that armor is rated 0/2/4/6 in V5. Do any of the supplement have armor rated as an odd number? Over six in a fashion that might imply a Dexterity penalty scheme? Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>No current V5 supplements have any additional armor or weapon mechanics. Everything abides by the core rulebook's material. So there's nothing that gives those odd numbered ratings in an official capacity.<br /> <br /> Some thoughts based on V5's system balance, working from the existing systems and roll methodology:<br /> * Armor should abide by the rule of '1 minimum damage' in some way. There are very few things that will allow damage to round to 0 (Firewalker) or that negate all damage together (a level 5 Fortitude power). Armor also needs to figure out how to not be redundant with Fortitude (downgrading and reducing), or be overpowered with them stacking.<br /> * Penalizing only Dexterity will not have the effect that it did in Revised/V20, as Dexterity is much more rarely used in conflict pools (the default use of Dex in conflict only in one-handed melee weapons and raw dodging, which isn't a pool used in every conflict).<br /> * Weapon damage scales in the manner it does because it's a roll-off system, so damage in and of itself has a scale based on the capabilities of the user, outside of the automatic successes on damage/. On averages, every 2 dots/dice = 1 successes. So if armor negates the damage bonus of weapons, you end up with the characters' raw skill being more important in damage and that will probably skew aspects of the system.<br /> * The system averages swing as you get more and more dice in a pool (this is why elders get scary with both passive and active dice adds).<br /> <br /> Just running some average numbers on just making armor equal damage reduction, armor would negate the bonuses of weapons plus some, leaving skill and supernatural capabilities as really the 'edge'. Potence would be even more useful than it is now. Fortitude's physical damage mitigation becomes overpowered if it stacks 1 for 1 with Armor damage reduction (someone with Armor 6 and Fortitude 3 is subtracting 9 damage min 1 from all incoming attacks), so you're going to be relying a lot on fishing for critical success. Cutting the amount of damage reduction would perhaps make it more balanced/viable, but basic stacking is going to end up with some levels of functional invincibility in a straight on fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 04-27-2020, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:32:50-07:00","id":1384320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384310#post1384310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Armor also needs to figure out how to not be redundant with Fortitude (downgrading and reducing), or be overpowered with them stacking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how easy that would be to do, as this is already somewhat the case.<br /> <br /> Do you think something like Storypath's Hard Armor might be a better place to go? Storypath's Hard Armor (it has Hard and Soft that have different effects) is extra Health boxes that take damage first from non-sunlight sources, and can't be healed. So instead of downgrading damage like armor does now to keep it simple, or mixed if a bit of complexity feels better in action, you'd get 1 to 3 extra Health. It doesn't seem like it would be overpowered with Fortitude, even if Fortitude + heaviest armor would be a lot of Health.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * Penalizing only Dexterity will not have the effect that it did in Revised/V20, as Dexterity is much more rarely used in conflict pools (the default use of Dex in conflict only in one-handed melee weapons and raw dodging, which isn't a pool used in every conflict). </div> </div> </div>This doesn't really bother me... Dexterity penalties in previous editions had a lot of odd effects compared to how cumbersome armor is. I used it in my house rule because V5 uses it for heavier armor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if armor negates the damage bonus of weapons, you end up with the characters' raw skill being more important in damage and that will probably skew aspects of the system. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure having skill mattering more if opponents come in with roughly equal equipment is a problem. I'd be more concerned with equipment cutting too far into skill mattering in uneven situations.<br /> <br /> What parts of the system would get skewed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just running some average numbers on just making armor equal damage reduction,... </div> </div> </div>Those numbers would clearly be too high. I don't think anyone's suggested just using the numbers as-is for direct damage reduction but instead lowering the reduction amount by some calculation to something less than armor value.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:56:53-07:00","id":1384335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384320#post1384320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure how easy that would be to do, as this is already somewhat the case.<br /> <br /> Do you think something like Storypath's Hard Armor might be a better place to go? Storypath's Hard Armor (it has Hard and Soft that have different effects) is extra Health boxes that take damage first from non-sunlight sources, and can't be healed. So instead of downgrading damage like armor does now to keep it simple, or mixed if a bit of complexity feels better in action, you'd get 1 to 3 extra Health. It doesn't seem like it would be overpowered with Fortitude, even if Fortitude + heaviest armor would be a lot of Health.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an option. The maximum health you can get by default in V5 is 13, Stam 5 Fort 5 +3 for calculation, which is much better than stacked damage reduction. IT doesn't feel like an insurmountable amount of health, though high BP healing might skew it (but that's a rarer case than just using the armor for standard fights). I would still keep the agg-to-superficial conversion of armor though, as that's the balancing factor for humans wearing it, since that doesn't really change. It would prolong a fight but nto as much as 'reduce by ARM rating, then reduce by fort and half'. Maybe something like 'armor eats 1 damage off of an attack, up to a number of attacks equal to it's rating, before it's capability to fully absorb damage is used up; however, the armor is still strong enough to convert agg to superficial, even if it's shattered state'. <br /> <br /> The most recent version of the MET LARP rules had one of the potential armor traits that reduced damage from one attack by 2 (so basically 2 Health Levels) that you could choose when to utilize, but once they were used up, they were used up until that item was replaced or repaired. Honestly, that version of the LARP rules wouldn't be a bad idea to mine stuff from, as it functioned on traits for other types of bonuses than just 'this armor absorbs damage' or 'this armor downgrades damage'. You had some traits like things that made staking difficult, negated special effects like knockback/knockdown, and a couple of others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What parts of the system would get skewed? </div> </div> </div>Basically you get into issues of hypercompetency when you add a lot of extra dice. I'd have to find the post again where I posted a bunch of dice math, but basically once you add a certain number of dice (it's like in the 17 total dice range) without the opposition having a similar scale, then it's essentially a one-sided conflict on roll averages with low statistical chances for the person with significantly less dice to win. Or if everyone is hypercompetent you get into issues of rocket tag. That was mainly what I was meaning, with some options like the way MET had traits to add bonus dice to defense against guns or melee, depending on what traits the armor had.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those numbers would clearly be too high. I don't think anyone's suggested just using the numbers as-is for direct damage reduction but instead lowering the reduction amount by some calculation to something less than armor value. </div> </div> </div>And that's fine, it was more of just pointing out 'using the numbers as written is going to lead to unexpected results and functional invulnerability, more or less. Need to start from the top and know how those numbers work, to be able to craft what numbers work on the lower end.<br /> <br /> Also, in regards to armor Prowess ignores 1 point of armor per level of Potence in addition to its extra damage; how would you make that work/balance in an armor that reduces damage? If Potence ignores the Armor DR used RAW, then Potence becomes a win condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 04-27-2020, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T21:39:44-07:00","id":1384352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384320#post1384320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure how easy that would be to do, as this is already somewhat the case.<br /> <br /> Do you think something like Storypath's Hard Armor might be a better place to go? Storypath's Hard Armor (it has Hard and Soft that have different effects) is extra Health boxes that take damage first from non-sunlight sources, and can't be healed. So instead of downgrading damage like armor does now to keep it simple, or mixed if a bit of complexity feels better in action, you'd get 1 to 3 extra Health. It doesn't seem like it would be overpowered with Fortitude, even if Fortitude + heaviest armor would be a lot of Health.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't mind something like this. <br /> <br /> Currently I was thinking of a system where armor reduces aggravated to superficial like it does now and gives the wearer halve its rating in non-healable health levels. The armor itself owns those levels and they can be repaired but not healed with a blood surge or regeneration for example. In normal combat the armor takes damage first and when damage upgrades it is the first to take the upgraded damage as well. Armor that loses it final box to aggravated damage is useless and beyond repair. This means that you can get 2 extra health boxes with a vest if you want which I am good with but the armor can also be worn down and degraded which is also nice in a dark ages setting wher you would need to have your armor repaired at a smithy or the like which feels thematic.<br /> <br /> As for the Dex penalty we already have this with military armor, which gives a 1 die penalty so I don't think there is a problem with Dex penalties either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T00:22:53-07:00","id":1384373,"title":"","content":"I think we should stay on topic, but then again the first comment on this thread was used to express displeasure that I made a V5 thread without regard to it's contents so...<br /> <br /> Look, V5's combat system where it's all-or-nothing who can attack best is interesting. It's fun if you don't really look into it too much or explore physical disciplines (That's a whole other can of worms) It allows for very fast combat and some people will be delighted to have that.<br /> <br /> But, objectively speaking, V5's armour system is unintuitive (what do you mean this doesn't protect me at all?) and unreal to an extent that greatly surpasses prior editions. A vampire does not gain any protection from swords, guns, bombs, stakes, arrows, hammers whatsoever; Three inches of steel might as well be thin women's clothing. Being &quot;too cool for armour&quot; should be the idiotic thought of neonates without expectations of reaching ancilae, not an actual game mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-28-2020, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T01:15:40-07:00","id":1384381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384373#post1384373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, objectively speaking, V5's armour system is unintuitive (what do you mean this doesn't protect me at all?) and unreal to an extent that greatly surpasses prior editions. A vampire does not gain any protection from swords, guns, bombs, stakes, arrows, hammers whatsoever; Three inches of steel might as well be thin women's clothing. Being &quot;too cool for armour&quot; should be the idiotic thought of neonates without expectations of reaching ancilae, not an actual game mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it\u2019s not an objective statement because, subjectively, I find the system entirely intuitive. Body armour converts a certain amount of aggravated damage into superficial damage. That is pretty intuitive to me. It\u2019s an opinion, which is valid, because all these qualitative statements about <i>intuition</i> are subjective not objective.<br /> <br /> Vampires don\u2019t gain any extra protection from armour against swords, guns, bombs and hammers because none of these things inflict aggravated damage against them. This is because they are vampires - magical undead beings. It\u2019s not a question of being 'too cool for armour\u2019 - which is a strawman argument because nobody suggested this - but a practical aspect of the functional use of armour largely being redundant for them.<br /> <br /> There is an argument, however, that vampires could gain some protection from armour against stakes (and arrows), insofar that these things can immobilize a vampire with called shots. It could be ruled (as a house rule) that strong armour might mitigate against this effect. You could also make an argument that body armour could, in theory at least, mitigate against the type of aggravated damage that does affect vampires - like werewolf claws or the like. In these cases, I would rule, that aggravated damage could be reduced to superficial damage in the same way that armour helps mortals against bullets, etc. It probably would have to come down to a house ruling on the matter, but it wouldn\u2019t take a lot of effort or difficulty to do so.<br /> <br /> For me, though, the whole debate here is overstated because armour is not something that normal mortals wear most of the time, either in the real world or in the stories I tell, and vampires are generally trying blend in with them in a typical, city based game. Vampires have inbuilt advantages that normal mortals don\u2019t have but mortals (and Thin Bloods) could mitigate against their disadvantages with equipment like body armour, or advanced weapons and tactics of various sorts. This is how I expect The Second Inquisition to work, and is essentially what the rules are trying to be presented as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-28-2020, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T01:19:29-07:00","id":1384382,"title":"","content":"The only thing that makes V5's armour system 'intuitive' is that &quot;superficial&quot; damage is called just, despite for vampires that could mean disembowlement or a missing arm, not just light bruising. So yeah, i can see how you'd get confused.<br /> <br /> <br /> But yeah, you try tell a player who knows about such things that their military body armour doesn't actually do anything. See how happy they are. Remember to remind them how 'intuitive' it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T01:56:11-07:00","id":1384385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384382#post1384382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that makes V5's armour system 'intuitive' is that &quot;superficial&quot; damage is called just, despite for vampires that could mean disembowlement or a missing arm, not just light bruising. So yeah, i can see how you'd get confused.<br /> <br /> But yeah, you try tell a player who knows about such things that their military body armour doesn't actually do anything. See how happy they are. Remember to remind them how 'intuitive' it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK. Will do. I\u2019m sure it will be received better than any conversation with someone who doesn\u2019t really know about such things, but just likes to complain a lot.<br /> <br /> Confounding your arguments is not the same thing as being confused, by the way. For a vampire, any damage that is superficial can be instantly repaired - at a rate determined by their Blood Potency - by rousing the blood. Impairment from superficial damage only occurs when the Health levels run out, and the damage suffered is halved, so the risk of disembowlement or a missing arm is somewhat overstated too. It\u2019s superficial, in fact.<br /> <br /> So, if a mortal gets shot with a shotgun for, say 8 points of aggravated damage, they are certainly incapacitated and most likely dead. If they wear heavy body armour that converts 6 points to superficial damage, they will probably survive at least, with maybe a bit of aggravated wounds and maybe impairment depending on their Health levels (based on Stamina). They would need medical attention and time to heal those extra Aggravated wounds, in any case.<br /> <br /> If a vampire took the same shot, without armour, they would only take 4 points of superficial damage and most likely no impairments unless they were especially low on Health levels. They could then Rouse the blood and instantly heal at least one of those wounds, depending on Blood Potency, and continue to do so each round if they wished.<br /> <br /> So, in all, Vampires still have the better deal by far, and armour in this circumstance is largely redundant for them. This is because they are fictional, magical beings. I am certain that a player who knows about such things would appreciate that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-28-2020, 05:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T03:26:36-07:00","id":1384389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384381#post1384381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is an argument, however, that vampires could gain some protection from armour against stakes (and arrows), insofar that these things can immobilize a vampire with called shots. It could be ruled (as a house rule) that strong armour might mitigate against this effect. You could also make an argument that body armour could, in theory at least, mitigate against the type of aggravated damage that does affect vampires - like werewolf claws or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Side note: Werewolf claws, very much like Feral Weapons (Protean 2), deal unhalved Superficial Damage, not Aggravated Damage to vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384381#post1384381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In these cases, I would rule, that aggravated damage could be reduced to superficial damage in the same way that armour helps mortals against bullets, etc. It probably would have to come down to a house ruling on the matter, but it wouldn\u2019t take a lot of effort or difficulty to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question: How would you rule the effects of a stab vest on a vampire, trying to protect himself against being staked?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384381#post1384381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, though, the whole debate here is overstated because armour is not something that normal mortals wear most of the time, either in the real world or in the stories I tell, and vampires are generally trying blend in with them in a typical, city based game. Vampires have inbuilt advantages that normal mortals don\u2019t have but mortals (and Thin Bloods) could mitigate against their disadvantages with equipment like body armour, or advanced weapons and tactics of various sorts. This is how I expect The Second Inquisition to work, and is essentially what the rules are trying to be presented as.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that and yes, I also think that armor is not that big of a problem. However, even in the design space of V5, one would assume to find players who enjoy action-heavy anarch games with night time raids on camarilla elders, using every tool they could get to even the odds. If the point of the debate is to only rant about V5, I guess there is no need to engage with it, but for me at least, it seems there are genuinely interested participants who would like to have a rules-tweak to provide vampires with a bonus when using armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25558-pangur-b\u00e1n","name":"Pangur B\u00e1n","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T03:44:50-07:00","id":1384390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pangur B\u00e1n</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384389#post1384389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Side note: Werewolf claws, very much like Feral Weapons (Protean 2), deal unhalved Superficial Damage, not Aggravated Damage to vampires.<br /> <br /> Question: How would you rule the effects of a stab vest on a vampire, trying to protect himself against being staked?</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019ll note that both of these things, which I hope I communicated, were just musings on house rules rather than official rules. In terms of how likely I would personally use rules like these is pretty hypothetical to me, as most of the stories I would be involved in wouldn\u2019t really be worrying about the impact of body armour. In the games I have been involved in, Werewolves are generally kept as ephemeral threats rather than regular encounters too.<br /> <br /> That said, in answer to your question, I would alter the stake damage rules, if somebody has specifically chosen to wear body armour to resist being staked, by ruling it can negate damage up to half of the rating of the armour. Staking is a called shot, so if somebody doesn\u2019t make a called shot, then the normal rules about armour would apply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get that and yes, I also think that armor is not that big of a problem. However, even in the design space of V5, one would assume to find players who enjoy action-heavy anarch games with night time raids on camarilla elders, using every tool they could get to even the odds. If the point of the debate is to only rant about V5, I guess there is no need to engage with it, but for me at least, it seems there are genuinely interested participants who would like to have a rules-tweak to provide vampires with a bonus when using armor. </div> </div> </div>Its the sort of rules discussion that could be written into a Players Guide certainly. The issue, for me, I guess is the tone of it - your own postings (which are perfectly fine), notwithstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T04:56:08-07:00","id":1384393,"title":"","content":"Yes, OP, v5 amour is useless. You have no system reward for wearing a kevlar or even a full armour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T07:13:17-07:00","id":1384405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384385#post1384385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK. Will do. I\u2019m sure it will be received better than any conversation with someone who doesn\u2019t really know about such things, but just likes to complain a lot..</div> </div> </div> </div>Because why settle for rational debate when you can just make snide remarks about the other party? Why do you feel the need to do that? <br /> <br /> I find it funny you chose a <i>shotgun</i> of all things to talk about how armour works, because assuming you're not using a slug those things are terribly ineffective against armour, especially considering the absurd amount of force those things can muster. At worst, you'd get a broken rib at point blank. Which is nothing compared to part of your chest turning into spaghetti. If only there were a mechanical difference between a bruise and a gaping hole. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T07:58:41-07:00","id":1384411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384405#post1384405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because why settle for rational debate when you can just make snide remarks about the other party? Why do you feel the need to do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019ve been making snide remarks - and your entire tone regarding anything to do with V5 is snide. You aren\u2019t in much of a position to lecture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I find it funny you chose a <i>shotgun</i> of all things to talk about how armour works, because assuming you're not using a slug those things are terribly ineffective against armour, especially considering the absurd amount of force those things can muster. At worst, you'd get a broken rib at point blank. Which is nothing compared to part of your chest turning into spaghetti. If only there were a mechanical difference between a bruise and a gaping hole. </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not sure what point you are trying to make. The example given shows quite clearly how a lethal shot is converted by armour, in the rules, to something that could be survived. A broken rib would be a good example of the extra aggravated damage suffered over the 6 threshold points of damage converted from aggravated to superficial. Had the shot delivered a full 8 points of aggravated damage, the target would be dead. So, the example shows there is a very clear mechanical difference between a bruise and a gaping hole. What you can\u2019t seem to accept, beyond this, is that what happens to a mortal body is not the same thing that happens to a vampire, which is a supernatural being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-28-2020, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T08:41:30-07:00","id":1384414,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2517_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2517\" data-vbnamecard=\"2517\">Trippy</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a><br /> <br /> If you have comments to report, report them. From now on, we're enforcing Elysium rules on this forum. Please treat other posters with respect. The edition wars are over. Some people like other editions and others don't. But if you feel another poster is being hostile, please do it through the mods. That's what we're here for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-