s-useless?p=1384414#post1384414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2517_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2517\" data-vbnamecard=\"2517\">Trippy</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a><br /> <br /> If you have comments to report, report them. From now on, we're enforcing Elysium on rules. Please treat other posters with respect. The edition wars are over. Some people like other editions and others don't. But if you feel another poster is being hostile, please do it through the mods. That's what we're here for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> man I know sooner or later that i am going to get doxed like many of us here. but I do have to say I am loving the initiative, it is great you all are stepping up to this and trying to fix it. and I will strive to comply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T09:34:42-07:00","id":1384429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384414#post1384414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2517_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2517\" data-vbnamecard=\"2517\">Trippy</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a><br /> <br /> If you have comments to report, report them. From now on, we're enforcing Elysium rules on this forum. Please treat other posters with respect. The edition wars are over. Some people like other editions and others don't. But if you feel another poster is being hostile, please do it through the mods. That's what we're here for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully it'll be enforced evenly, rather than the pretty thinly veiled 'it's just bashing on V5, so let it continue' slide that has been prevalent on the forums for months and months.<br /> <br /> Back on topic, I'm going to try to run numbers via statistics dice bot on how much armor being extra HL (running wit ha default of 2, and running with a default of half it's rating) will skew conflict. I'll probably have some numbers tomorrow for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T12:34:15-07:00","id":1384474,"title":"","content":"I don't like V5, but that really doesn't have anything to say about the topic at hand. Even if I did like V5, armour would still be useless to vampires. Wether or not I like V5 has no impact on the usefulness of armour in the setting. <br /> <br /> It's quite clear, plain as day, that armour doesn't do anything. Let's look at the following scenario: I'll acount for V5 vampires not having the durable bodies of prior editions. Let's say there's Greg and Gale. Both are fit and have 3 stamina, but Gale is a vampire who possesses disciplines of relevance to this test. If we took a 12 guage shotgun loaded with buckshot and shot at them from three metres towards their centre of mass, and then compared them to alternate versions of themselves wearing NIJ rated IIIA armour, we'd should expect something like this<br /> <br /> Greg the human shot without armour- Big fist sized spaghetti wound. Very dead. <br /> Gale the Vampire shot without armour- Big fist sized Spaghetti wound. Very hurt but not about to meet final death. Probably stunned <br /> <br /> Greg the human shot with armour- Hurt. Maybe a Broken rib. Probably stunned for a round or so.<br /> Gale the vampire shot with armour- The armour absorbs the majority of the force and the remainder is not enough to bother someone who can withstand part of his chest turned into spaghetti. <br /> <br /> But, mechanically, in v5 Gale suffers the same, spaghetti wound or not. <br /> If we went medieval here, we could use a sword against a man in chain. If he wore chain, you wouldn't be able to cut through him. But whilst the mortal gets benefits from chain, again, the vampire gets nothing. Hacking an arm off is more difficult to do against an armoured greg, but no more difficult against an armoured gale. <br /> <br /> In prior editions of the game. We'd have a conflict like such<br /> Str+Potence+weapon+Carry over VS Stamina+Fortitude+armour. The carry over could be dealt proactively by defending, otherwise this was a rather even conflict. Infact neither stamina nor fortitude nor armour made the others redunandant: They would build on top of eachother in an entirely organic manner. But In V5 we have carry over+weapon or potence VS... Fortitude if you've got it. <br /> <br /> Armour in V5 doesn't do it's job. It doesn't fit it's purpose. Steel and kevlar literally might as well be paper. I don't think it works great for mortals either, but it does still kinda work for them with the abstract combat system V5 has. But for vampires, it's a bad joke. And from a player standpoint, it's infuriating to have something work well for others but not for you solely because of someone's strange notions of balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T13:12:39-07:00","id":1384486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384429#post1384429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hopefully it'll be enforced evenly, rather than the pretty thinly veiled 'it's just bashing on V5, so let it continue' slide that has been prevalent on the forums for months and months</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't shit on anyone's favorite edition. You can dislike one but don't compare it to Tzimisce Vicissituding your balls off. Don't shit on fellow posters. If you have a problem with the latter, report the post and let the mods handle it. Assume we're all fans here.<br /> <br /> Pretty easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T13:32:18-07:00","id":1384491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384474#post1384474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greg the human shot without armour- Big fist sized spaghetti wound. Very dead.<br /> Gale the Vampire shot without armour- Big fist sized Spaghetti wound. Very hurt but not about to meet final death. Probably stunned<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if that's true. I remember some flavor text, admittedly from older editions, about what soaking meant. And it gave multiple options, such as the blood literally holding a severed limb on, like some cross between a T-1000 and Spider-Man's web shooting out. And that was just one of the options mentioned. Vampires taking less damage from a bullet doesn't necessarily mean being like a zombie, taking the same wound and caring about it less than a human. It CAN mean that, but it doesn't have to, and that's not always the appropriate option.<br /> <br /> Maybe vampire flesh just doesn't react to bullets the same way, suffering only a neat little puncture from a bullet that would create a gory exit wound on a human.<br /> <br /> Maybe vampire flesh DOES react normally, but the blood does a certain percentage of instantaneous healing even without rousing the blood or fortitude. Maybe the blood itself imperfectly replaces damaged tissue, as if the vampire immediately becomes part T-1000 without even rousing the blood. Regardless, vampire's superhuman soak can mean whatever the ST wants it to mean.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T13:45:06-07:00","id":1384492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384474#post1384474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like V5, but that really doesn't have anything to say about the topic at hand. Even if I did like V5, armour would still be useless to vampires. Wether or not I like V5 has no impact on the usefulness of armour in the setting.<br /> <br /> It's quite clear, plain as day, that armour doesn't do anything. Let's look at the following scenario: I'll acount for V5 vampires not having the durable bodies of prior editions. Let's say there's Greg and Gale. Both are fit and have 3 stamina, but Gale is a vampire who possesses disciplines of relevance to this test. If we took a 12 guage shotgun loaded with buckshot and shot at them from three metres towards their centre of mass, and then compared them to alternate versions of themselves wearing NIJ rated IIIA armour, we'd should expect something like this<br /> <br /> Greg the human shot without armour- Big fist sized spaghetti wound. Very dead.<br /> Gale the Vampire shot without armour- Big fist sized Spaghetti wound. Very hurt but not about to meet final death. Probably stunned<br /> <br /> Greg the human shot with armour- Hurt. Maybe a Broken rib. Probably stunned for a round or so.<br /> Gale the vampire shot with armour- The armour absorbs the majority of the force and the remainder is not enough to bother someone who can withstand part of his chest turned into spaghetti.<br /> <br /> But, mechanically, in v5 Gale suffers the same, spaghetti wound or not.<br /> If we went medieval here, we could use a sword against a man in chain. If he wore chain, you wouldn't be able to cut through him. But whilst the mortal gets benefits from chain, again, the vampire gets nothing. Hacking an arm off is more difficult to do against an armoured greg, but no more difficult against an armoured gale.<br /> <br /> In prior editions of the game. We'd have a conflict like such<br /> Str+Potence+weapon+Carry over VS Stamina+Fortitude+armour. The carry over could be dealt proactively by defending, otherwise this was a rather even conflict. Infact neither stamina nor fortitude nor armour made the others redunandant: They would build on top of eachother in an entirely organic manner. But In V5 we have carry over+weapon or potence VS... Fortitude if you've got it.<br /> <br /> Armour in V5 doesn't do it's job. It doesn't fit it's purpose. Steel and kevlar literally might as well be paper. I don't think it works great for mortals either, but it does still kinda work for them with the abstract combat system V5 has. But for vampires, it's a bad joke. And from a player standpoint, it's infuriating to have something work well for others but not for you solely because of someone's strange notions of balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couple of things in previous editions you would not add strength and potence to a ranged weapons damage. nor would you add potence to it in V5,<br /> <br /> Vampires in V5 were giving Armor infinity by their very nature, why would giving them 2 more points mater? That just doesn't make since. The whole of this argument is comparing apples to oranges. The systems are not the same do not have the same design goals nor the same math behind a dice pools success ratio just due to changes in difficulty. In earlier editions you have soak in V5 you half non-aggravated damage automatically.<br /> <br /> Surface comparisons don't prove anything and even the point of this thread seems futile. Is the purpose to make V5 look bad? What's the point of even bringing it up?<br /> <br /> In V5 you gained infinate armor wooo hooo. in previous edition you got to soak damage, woo hooo. Why does it matter? if the point is to find something that works better for you game then we have thrown out several methods for doing so. or hey just add soaking damage back in if you wish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T13:55:22-07:00","id":1384495,"title":"","content":"Simply put, Kevlar armour and the like is designed to protect mortals from lethal damage. It is not designed to protect vampires from anything particularly - because vampires are clandestine, supernatural creatures and not at the forefront of the priorities for Kevlar manufacture in the mortal world. Vampires have their own supernatural defenses, and essentially make mortal-designed defenses redundant - because they are magic. If they wanted to find an alternative to mortal armour for themselves, the design would also most likely be magic. Magic trumps physics in a fictional world.<br /> <br /> Mortal armour isn\u2019t particularly useful for zombies or ghosts either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-28-2020, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T14:22:07-07:00","id":1384508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384495#post1384495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mortal armour isn\u2019t particularly useful for zombies or ghosts either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Armour is more useful for Zombies, they only have to care about breaks, amputations and brain damage which body armour prevents...a Z in full military class 4 is a freaking juggernaut, (assuming Romeo zombies), for exactly the reason a vampire should be,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T14:32:19-07:00","id":1384510,"title":"","content":"OK, since we're still debating some core issues, anyone that would like to defend the RAW:<br /> <br /> Please explain why a mortal or a ghoul wearing riot armor vs. a mortal/ghoul with a baseball bat wearing street clothing is actually at a mechanical disadvantage.<br /> <br /> As it stands, riot armor, which is designed to protect police from frequently improvised weapons many of which would count as superficial damage even to mortals, has no impact against a baseball bat (superficial source of damage that it is) despite being designed specifically to combat such attacks.<br /> <br /> So armor vs. unarmored with equal weapons (a police baton vs. a bat) seems like a wash on equipment; which is already strange enough.<br /> <br /> However, riot armor, being the high end armor also has a -1 Dexterity dice pool penalty. So, wearing armor specifically meant to protect you from blunt trauma, in V5, impedes you instead of aids you, if you're a mortal/ghoul facing already superficial sources of blunt trauma. Mortals and ghouls are not vampires. They do not have the defense of magically powered corpse-bodies to explain this.<br /> <br /> As for as issues of relevance to the game: imagine how this plays out for the tactics of the Anarchs, Sabbat, and Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> A Brujah Anarch that has the ability to rile up local unrest to the point of a full on riot isn't just creating a big mess that puts Camarilla assets at risk, that Anarch is generating an effective army that's mechanically better off than the riot police that show up to stop them. Unless the cops are going to start using lethal force, they're going to get steamrolled by the mechanically superior rioters. The Anarch can use the chaos of the rioters winning to torch Camarilla Havens and assets without the Camarilla having the resources of control over local mortals to help protect them. Or the Camarilla can pressure the police into turning their city into a war-zone, making it easier for the SI to infiltrate their city as the government puts civil liberties aside to reassert order.<br /> <br /> So, Anarchs stoking civil unrest, and things like Sabbat mass embrace tactics are more dangerous than ever, because mortal police forces got nerfed by way the armor rules work.<br /> <br /> If someone can present a logical reason why riot armor shouldn't protect a mortal from being punched/hit with a baseball bat/have a rock thrown at you/etc. please, present it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T14:52:02-07:00","id":1384514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384510#post1384510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, since we're still debating some core issues, anyone that would like to defend the RAW:<br /> <br /> Please explain why a mortal or a ghoul wearing riot armor vs. a mortal/ghoul with a baseball bat wearing street clothing is actually at a mechanical disadvantage.<br /> <br /> As it stands, riot armor, which is designed to protect police from frequently improvised weapons many of which would count as superficial damage even to mortals, has no impact against a baseball bat (superficial source of damage that it is) despite being designed specifically to combat such attacks.<br /> <br /> So armor vs. unarmored with equal weapons (a police baton vs. a bat) seems like a wash on equipment; which is already strange enough.<br /> <br /> However, riot armor, being the high end armor also has a -1 Dexterity dice pool penalty. So, wearing armor specifically meant to protect you from blunt trauma, in V5, impedes you instead of aids you, if you're a mortal/ghoul facing already superficial sources of blunt trauma. Mortals and ghouls are not vampires. They do not have the defense of magically powered corpse-bodies to explain this.<br /> <br /> As for as issues of relevance to the game: imagine how this plays out for the tactics of the Anarchs, Sabbat, and Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> A Brujah Anarch that has the ability to rile up local unrest to the point of a full on riot isn't just creating a big mess that puts Camarilla assets at risk, that Anarch is generating an effective army that's mechanically better off than the riot police that show up to stop them. Unless the cops are going to start using lethal force, they're going to get steamrolled by the mechanically superior rioters. The Anarch can use the chaos of the rioters winning to torch Camarilla Havens and assets without the Camarilla having the resources of control over local mortals to help protect them. Or the Camarilla can pressure the police into turning their city into a war-zone, making it easier for the SI to infiltrate their city as the government puts civil liberties aside to reassert order.<br /> <br /> So, Anarchs stoking civil unrest, and things like Sabbat mass embrace tactics are more dangerous than ever, because mortal police forces got nerfed by way the armor rules work.<br /> <br /> If someone can present a logical reason why riot armor shouldn't protect a mortal from being punched/hit with a baseball bat/have a rock thrown at you/etc. please, present it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At this point everyone is just going around in circles. We know that the RAW are not close to realistic. The RAW are balanced within the internal mechanism of V5 as they are. Just like AC is balanced within D&amp;D's internal mechanisms. Just like any other system designed for any other game. I feel like everyone is beating a dead horse going bUt WhY at this point. The cases you're bringing up are probably things way outside the average ST's mind and modus operandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T14:55:46-07:00","id":1384515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384508#post1384508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Armour is more useful for Zombies, they only have to care about breaks, amputations and brain damage which body armour prevents...a Z in full military class 4 is a freaking juggernaut, (assuming Romeo zombies), for exactly the reason a vampire should be,</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think they <i>care </i>about these things, especially. However, in a more abstract sense, the main feature of a Zombie is they keep getting up against blows that would be lethal against mortals. A zombie in full military class 4 armour isn\u2019t at a greater advantage in this sense. You shoot against a zombie with armour and it keeps going. You shoot against a zombie without armour and it keeps going. You could target the head or some way of reducing its mobility, but if they somehow had protection in the form of a helmet or whatever, I\u2019d just increase the difficulty of a called shot accordingly - and have the effect be specific (like staking is for vampires). <br /> <br /> Any thoughts on a ghost using mortal armour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T15:01:25-07:00","id":1384517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384515#post1384515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t think they <i>care </i>about these things, especially. However, in a more abstract sense, the main feature of a Zombie is they keep getting up against blows that would be lethal against mortals. A zombie in full military class 4 armour isn\u2019t at a greater advantage in this sense. You shoot against a zombie with armour and it keeps going. You shoot against a zombie without armour and it keeps going. You could target the head or some way of reducing its mobility, but if they somehow had protection in the form of a helmet or whatever, I\u2019d just increase the difficulty of a called shot accordingly - and have the effect be specific (like staking is for vampires). <br /> <br /> Any thoughts on a ghost using mortal armour?</div> </div> </div> </div>'Care' emotionally no, ofc they don't, but broken limbs are still broken limbs, even without the associated bleeding and shock, they don't function properly, if at all, and armour helps prevent that damage.<br /> <br /> Ghosts in mortal armour: one of the most durable objects to possess (assuming animating a statue is not an option) and a horror classic, the implacable empty suit, infused with the spirit of its former owner, or a sacrifice or an evil spirit etc, killing to avenge/protect/because it's fun. So yea it works really well, but not in the same way<br /> <br /> Someone thinking of getting into a serious conflict should be thinking of armour with the same focus they apply to automatic weapons, incendaries and explosives, it works, it makes the mission more possible, and more survivable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-28-2020, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T15:12:10-07:00","id":1384519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384510#post1384510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone can present a logical reason why riot armor shouldn't protect a mortal from being punched/hit with a baseball bat/have a rock thrown at you/etc. please, present it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the system is abstract, then Health levels lost through these means don\u2019t necessarily mean a character is injured. If they are contained as superficial damage, then character will recover in the next session without any healing. It\u2019s only when Health levels are exhausted that impediment and possible aggravated damage will be incurred - maybe because the armour is considered to be breached at this point.<br /> <br /> If baseball bats or rocks are used proficiently, it could be argued that they can break bones and limbs, and are therefore possibly causing Aggravated damage - which would require medical attention and time to heal. As such, Riot armour would act to reduce this damage to superficial levels too. A straight punch would probably be rendered useless against riot armour, but the unarmed attack may not be a punch - but maybe a push or trip or something else. Again, the system is abstracted. What body armour does is protect the wearer from lethal, aggravated damage - not all forms of potential damage. If a riot officer was also using a large shield, as they often do, I\u2019d also give them bonuses for blocking the attack. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T15:18:42-07:00","id":1384520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384517#post1384517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'Care' emotionally no, ofc they don't, but broken limbs are still broken limbs, even without the associated bleeding and shock, they don't function properly, if at all, and armour helps prevent that damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that is an impairment isn\u2019t it? It\u2019s not lethal or aggravated. If you blow a zombie up into a mess of rendered limbs, they keep moving. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever seen a Zombie going into shock in any movie I\u2019ve ever seen. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ghosts in mortal armour: one of the most durable objects to possess (assuming animating a statue is not an option) and a horror classic, the implacable empty suit, infused with the spirit of its former owner, or a sacrifice or an evil spirit etc, killing to avenge/protect/because it's fun. So yea it works really well, but not in the same way </div> </div> </div>Not really. Even if the armour is animated by the ghost, any attack to the armour has no bearing on the ghost. The ghost, by WoD definitions, is incorporeal, meaning mortal armour is irrelevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Someone thinking of getting into a serious conflict should be thinking of armour with the same focus they apply to automatic weapons, incendaries and explosives, it works, it makes the mission more possible, and more survivable. </div> </div> </div>A vampire looking to get into serious conflict would probably need to look beyond mortal means of defense. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T15:34:58-07:00","id":1384521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384520#post1384520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that is an impairment isn\u2019t it? It\u2019s not lethal or aggravated. If you blow a zombie up into a mess of rendered limbs, they keep moving. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever seen a Zombie going into shock in any movie I\u2019ve ever seen. <br /> <br /> Not really. Even if the armour is animated by the ghost, any attack to the armour has no bearing on the ghost. The ghost, by WoD definitions, is incorporeal, meaning mortal armour is irrelevant.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Blowing a zombie to pieces slows it even further, shattered limbs and spine stop it moving as fast, and enough damage stops it moving at all, armour helps prevent that turning something extremely durable into something damn near unstoppable. (Left 4 Dead, World War Z (the book) and the Dead series all have examples of that, armour is more useful for creatures that don't fear bruising, concussion etc, not less.<br /> <br /> As to ghosts yup, the ghost itself probably won't be harmed by destroying its host object ( depending if the object is what binds it to undeath or not for instance) but having armour be a super tough host is totally a horror trope.<br /> <br /> As to defense beyond mortal, sure you should be looking at ways to stop Dominate etc, but ways to stop bullets, blades and blunt trauma already exist, it's called armour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T15:43:44-07:00","id":1384523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384521#post1384521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blowing a zombie to pieces slows it even further, shattered limbs and spine stop it moving as fast, and enough damage stops it moving at all, armour helps prevent that turning something extremely durable into something damn near unstoppable. (Left 4 Dead, World War Z (the book) and the Dead series all have examples of that, armour is more useful for creatures that don't fear bruising, concussion etc, not less.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but do you allow for a zombie to have all the smashed bits slowly find each other and reassemble? Some fictional representations have them doing that. It is difficult to assess how useful armour is for fictional, supernatural beings because you can make the rules up as to how that supernatural power responds. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to ghosts yup, the ghost itself probably won't be harmed by destroying its host object ( depending if the object is what binds it to undeath or not for instance) but having armour be a super tough host is totally a horror trope. </div> </div> </div>Well, then that could be described as a magical item, which would have its own rules - it isn\u2019t the same thing as mortal armour. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to defense beyond mortal, sure you should be looking at ways to stop Dominate etc, but ways to stop bullets, blades and blunt trauma already exist, it's called armour. </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily mortal armour though. Supernatural beings have their own methods of defense. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T15:52:03-07:00","id":1384525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384523#post1384523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)Ah, but do you allow for a zombie to have all the smashed bits slowly find each other and reassemble? Some fictional representations have them doing that. It is difficult to assess how useful armour is for fictional, supernatural beings because you can make the rules up as to how that supernatural power responds. <br /> <br /> 2)Well, then that could be described as a magical item, which would have its own rules - it isn\u2019t the same thing as mortal armour. <br /> <br /> 3)Not necessarily mortal armour though. Supernatural beings have their own methods of defense. </div> </div> </div> </div>1)if they are allowed to reform, armour still makes them more effective than not having it, damage that doesn't happen is better than damage that has to heal/reform.<br /> <br /> 2) which is why I didn't address ghosts originally, they truly are a separate issue.<br /> <br /> 3) not with out completely changing WoD lore they don't. (And indeed several modern classic portrayals of vampires) as well as logic and physics, damage prevented is better than damage endured (and Vamps having lost the ability to 'no sell' damage this edition makes that a more, not less vital point) being cherry tapped down by gun fire is easier this edition not harder, Gehenna has made Vamps more vulnerable to bullets, not less, armour is more needed now.(if it actually worked in a coherent way, which it does not)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T16:06:44-07:00","id":1384527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384525#post1384525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)if they are allowed to reform, armour still makes them more effective than not having it, damage that doesn't happen is better than damage that has to heal/reform.<br /> <br /> 2) which is why I didn't address ghosts originally, they truly are a separate issue.<br /> <br /> 3) not with out completely changing WoD lore they don't. (And indeed several modern classic portrayals of vampires) as well as logic and physics, damage prevented is better than damage endured (and Vamps having lost the ability to 'no sell' damage this edition makes that a more, not less vital point) being cherry tapped down by gun fire is easier this edition not harder, Gehenna has made Vamps more vulnerable to bullets, not less, armour is more needed now.(if it actually worked in a coherent way, which it does not)</div> </div> </div> </div>Armour doesn\u2019t make zombies any more effective though, if lethal damage is just going to be rendered non-lethal regardless.<br /> <br /> And the point about ghosts is yes, they are a separate issue. But so are vampires, when considering mortal armour. <br /> <br /> WoD lore is that vampires are supernatural beings, where the physics of the real world are trumped by magic. The logic and physics you are asserting isn\u2019t vampire lore, it is just how you are trying to interpret it. There is nothing written about Gehenna in any WoD book I\u2019ve ever read, that made reference to the functionality of kevlar armour. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T20:39:21-07:00","id":1384556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384527#post1384527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)Armour doesn\u2019t make zombies any more effective though, if lethal damage is just going to be rendered non-lethal regardless.<br /> <br /> And the point about ghosts is yes, they are a separate issue. But so are vampires, when considering mortal armour. <br /> <br /> 2)WoD lore is that vampires are supernatural beings, where the physics of the real world are trumped by magic. The logic and physics you are asserting isn\u2019t vampire lore, it is just how you are trying to interpret it. There is nothing written about Gehenna in any WoD book I\u2019ve ever read, that made reference to the functionality of kevlar armour. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>except in every bit of fiction we have where the topic turns up, and in verisimilitude? Using the game mechanic that makes armour useless, to justify armour being useless is circular reasoning, armour should not be useless, it being so makes zero sense and damages suspension of disbelief, that is a bug, not a feature (and as pointed out earlier by another poster, brings up bizarre none edge cases like riot gear being useless for mortals, let alone vampires), and how things previously worked, vampires previously benefitted from armour, some of them wore it, during combat operations, now it is pointless, for reasons that make no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T20:50:59-07:00","id":1384558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384556#post1384556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> except in every bit of fiction we have where the topic turns up, and in verisimilitude?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, cite these examples in WoD fiction then. Where is kevlar armour mentioned in relation to Gehenna? In terms of verisimilitude, I guess that is what we are debating, but its not an absolute, its a matter of perspective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using the game mechanic that makes armour useless, to justify armour being useless is circular reasoning, armour should not be useless, it being so makes zero sense and damages suspension of disbelief, that is a bug, not a feature (and as pointed out earlier by another poster, brings up bizarre none edge cases like riot gear being useless for mortals, let alone vampires), and how things previously worked, vampires previously benefitted from armour, some of them wore it, during combat operations, now it is pointless, for reasons that make no sense. </div> </div> </div>But amour isn\u2019t useless in the V5 game mechanics - it converts Aggravated damage to Superficial damage, and can prevent a mortal character from dying. This does not suspend disbelief in the slightest, because that is what it does in reality.<br /> <br /> It is not useless when acting against non-projectile weapons that cause trauma either - a baseball bat or brick used effectively could be classified as something that causes Aggravated damage against a mortal, because they can be lethal, which can be reduced with Riot armour accordingly.<br /> <br /> When used by vampires it has a negligible effect, because vampires are supernatural beings that are undead. Damage that would normally be aggravated for mortals do not effect vampires, so body armour doesn\u2019t have any real function for them. It says this plainly in the rules too, along with the rationale.<br /> <br /> Previous editions\u2019 rules, as has been made clear by moderation, do not have any bearing or comparison to be made with the V5 rules on this thread. I could criticize them too, but that is not the purpose of this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-28-2020, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T21:13:42-07:00","id":1384562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384558#post1384558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, cite these examples in WoD fiction then. Where is kevlar armour mentioned in relation to Gehenna? In terms of verisimilitude, I guess that is what we are debating, but its not an absolute, its a matter of perspective.<br /> <br /> But amour isn\u2019t useless in the V5 game mechanics - it converts Aggravated damage to Superficial damage, and can prevent a mortal character from dying. This does not suspend disbelief in the slightest, because that is what it does in reality.<br /> <br /> It is not useless when acting against non-projectile weapons that cause trauma either - a baseball bat or brick used effectively could be classified as something that causes Aggravated damage against a mortal, because they can be lethal, which can be reduced with Riot armour accordingly.<br /> <br /> When used by vampires it has a negligible effect, because vampires are supernatural beings that are undead. Damage that would normally be aggravated for mortals do not effect vampires, so body armour doesn\u2019t have any real function for them. It says this plainly in the rules too, along with the rationale.<br /> <br /> Previous editions\u2019 rules, as has been made clear by moderation, do not have any bearing or comparison to be made with the V5 rules on this thread. I could criticize them too, but that is not the purpose of this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bloodlines for starters, apart from that pretty sure Karsh wears armour, and his strike teams certainly do, not going to go back thru the novels to find more. Referencing previous editions has to matter here, they are in the same universe, and supposedly you can tell the same stories using either system... except you cannot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T21:48:55-07:00","id":1384571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384562#post1384562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Bloodlines for starters, apart from that pretty sure Karsh wears armour, and his strike teams certainly do, not going to go back thru the novels to find more. Referencing previous editions has to matter here, they are in the same universe, and supposedly you can tell the same stories using either system... except you cannot</div> </div> </div> </div>Bloodlines is a videogame adaptation of Vampire as a game, which probably just uses previous editions' rules when it comes to armour - and we are avoiding comparing V5 to previous editions rules aren\u2019t we? Was there any reference made to Karsh, in books, wearing body armour that actually served to protect him with an example from text - as in his kevlar vest stopped him from taking a lethal blow? Is there any example from any novel of the use of body armour by vampires in action? Looking through the old Gangrel Clanbook doesn\u2019t seem to suggest anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-29-2020, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T21:51:48-07:00","id":1384572,"title":"","content":"Since it seems to come up routinely, I'd like to point something out: vampires are not zombies. Zombies function purely via indifference to damage. With vampires there is some utterly ambiguous combination of indifference to damage and magical properties of their blood. It's unclear how much they are like zombies and how much they are like T-1000's, but earlier editions implied at least a degree of T-1000ness to their ability to soak. Shoot a zombie in the elbow, and the arm is reduced in functionality. Shoot a vampire in the elbow, and maybe the arm is reduced in functionality, and maybe the blood holds it together and keeps it animated normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T22:32:11-07:00","id":1384575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384571#post1384571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bloodlines is a videogame adaptation of Vampire as a game, which probably just uses previous editions' rules when it comes to armour - and we are avoiding comparing V5 to previous editions rules aren\u2019t we? Was there any reference made to Karsh, in books, wearing body armour that actually served to protect him with an example from text - as in his kevlar vest stopped him from taking a lethal blow? Is there any example from any novel of the use of body armour by vampires in action? Looking through the old Gangrel Clanbook doesn\u2019t seem to suggest anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop trying to 'no true Scotsman' fallacy your way out of this. If we cannot use previous Masquerade stories to see what the world is like, why is the game called VtM? If it isn't the same universe why is it named as such? If this was a completely separate game, with a totally different setting, you may have a point, but your constant attempts to defend the indefensible are wearing thin. Their is no precedent in either the myths or the previous lore for armour doing nothing, their is for Vampires not caring about damage, and enduring pain as a mark of toughness or apathy, but not for it being worthless (apart from some myths with flat immunity to mortal weapons)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-29-2020, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T00:49:08-07:00","id":1384593,"title":"","content":"I also saw a ton of vampires wearing armour in the last DA book. But please, inform us, why wouldn't a device specifically designed to deflect or absorb traumatic wounds work at all for vampire? Not that vampires don't really 'need' it, but that it doesn't work for them. Because I feel like you're saying a castle wouldn't benefit from more and better defences here. <br /> <br /> Maybe your vission here is too hyper-specific for us common people who just think armour aught to do it's job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T01:37:21-07:00","id":1384597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384575#post1384575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stop trying to 'no true Scotsman' fallacy your way out of this. If we cannot use previous Masquerade stories to see what the world is like, why is the game called VtM? If it isn't the same universe why is it named as such? If this was a completely separate game, with a totally different setting, you may have a point, but your constant attempts to defend the indefensible are wearing thin. Their is no precedent in either the myths or the previous lore for armour doing nothing, their is for Vampires not caring about damage, and enduring pain as a mark of toughness or apathy, but not for it being worthless (apart from some myths with flat immunity to mortal weapons)</div> </div> </div> </div>It has nothing to do with \u2018no true Scostman' fallacy. It has everything to do with a moderator explicitly instructing on this thread that we should not be comparing previous editions to V5, in order to avoid edition warring. When I asked you to cite previous Masquerade stories, it is not a valid example to present me with a videogame version of the game, which is what Bloodlines is, that is based on a previous edition\u2019s rules. It\u2019s like citing V20 as an example of Masquerade story. I am asking for actual stories, not alternate game system references.<br /> <br /> Where are the examples of Masquerade stories where vampires need protection through body armour?<br /> <br /> And no, there is nothing indefensible about the V5 rules. That is just a Danth\u2019s Law fallacy.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of examples of vampires not needing to wear armour, as in they generally don\u2019t. Y\u2019know, I started checking out all the example characters from old splat books - which amounts to about 260 characters if you count them. How many do you think listed body armour in their equipment lists? And, again, armour is not useless in V5 - it\u2019s just pretty redundant for vampires who have their own means of protection already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-29-2020, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T01:39:40-07:00","id":1384598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384593#post1384593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also saw a ton of vampires wearing armour in the last DA book. But please, inform us, why wouldn't a device specifically designed to deflect or absorb traumatic wounds work at all for vampire? Not that vampires don't really 'need' it, but that it doesn't work for them. Because I feel like you're saying a castle wouldn't benefit from more and better defences here.<br /> <br /> Maybe your vission here is too hyper-specific for us common people who just think armour aught to do it's job.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Dark Ages is another case, as with any other era of the game. The V5 core book only caters for modern nights, and so the Dark Ages setting is outside of its remit. It could be a suggestion to expand on rules for other eras of play in upcoming Players Guide, where armour rules for medieval combat could also potentially be looked at.<br /> <br /> The reason why a device specifically designed to deflect or absorb traumatic wounds won\u2019t work at all for a vampire would be.....because it isn\u2019t specifically designed for a vampire. It is specifically designed for a mortal, and what constitutes traumatic wounds for a mortal is not the same for a vampire.<br /> <br /> For mortals, armour does its job. For vampires, its job is redundant to them because they already do what the armour does, better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-29-2020, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T01:54:25-07:00","id":1384599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384598#post1384598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Dark Ages is another case, as with any other era of the game. The V5 core book only caters for modern nights, and so the Dark Ages setting is outside of its remit. It could be a suggestion to expand on rules for other eras of play in upcoming Players Guide, where armour rules for medieval combat could also potentially be looked at.<br /> <br /> The reason why a device specifically designed to deflect or absorb traumatic wounds work at all for a vampire would be.....because it isn\u2019t specifically designed for a vampire. It is specifically designed for a mortal, and what constitutes traumatic wounds for a mortal is not the same for a vampire.<br /> <br /> For mortals, armour does its job. For vampires, its job is redundant to them because they already do what the armour does, better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> that makes zero sense. Like none at all. Literally it breaks disbelief totally, if vampires work like that..they aren't vampires, they are something else entirely,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384597#post1384597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has nothing to do with \u2018no true Scostman' fallacy. It has everything to do with a moderator explicitly instructing on this thread that we should not be comparing previous editions to V5, in order to avoid edition warring. When I asked you to cite previous Masquerade stories, it is not a valid example to present me with a videogame version of the game, which is what Bloodlines is, that is based on a previous edition\u2019s rules. It\u2019s like citing V20 as an example of Masquerade story. I am asking for actual stories, not alternate game system references.<br /> <br /> Where are the examples of Masquerade stories where vampires need protection through body armour?<br /> <br /> And no, there is nothing indefensible about the V5 rules. That is just a Danth\u2019s Law fallacy.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of examples of vampires not needing to wear armour, as in they generally don\u2019t. Y\u2019know, I started checking out all the example characters from old splat books - which amounts to about 260 characters if you count them. How many do you think listed body armour in their equipment lists? And, again, armour is not useless in V5 - it\u2019s just pretty redundant for vampires who have their own means of protection already.</div> </div> </div> </div>IT was, I provided examples which you dismissed as not being 'true examples' even tho it is the military commander of the Camirilla and his elite forces using military equipment, apparently that example doesn't count. Given the cherry tap system, of 1 minimum damage now, killing vampires with gun fire has never been easier, so they should be piling on the trauma plates...except for some reason stopping a bullet before it hits your flesh does them no good. So given that they are harmed equally whether a bullet strikes them or not, should they be taking damage from misses now as well?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-29-2020, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T02:04:46-07:00","id":1384601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384599#post1384599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that makes zero sense. Like none at all. Literally it breaks disbelief totally, if vampireas work like that..they aren't vampires, they are something else entirely,</div> </div> </div> </div>And that isn\u2019t really an argument. If vampires work like what, they aren\u2019t vampires?<br /> <br /> Vampires are vampires because they are supernatural creatures that feed off blood - which provides them with supernatural power. They are definitely not mortal and, as such, have different qualities to mortals - including their supernatural resistance to lethal damage. Armour designed to protect mortals from lethal damage, accordingly, won\u2019t necessarily be useful to a vampire, in the same respect it wouldn\u2019t be useful to a ghost or Superman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> IT was, I provided examples which you dismissed as not being 'true examples' even tho it is the military commander of the Camirilla and his elite forces using military equipment, apparently that example doesn't count. Given the cherry tap system, of 1 minimum damage now, killing vampires with gun fire has never been easier, so they should be piling on the trauma plates...except for some reason stopping a bullet before it hits your flesh does them no good. So given that they are harmed equally whether a bullet strikes them or not, should they be taking damage from misses now as well? </div> </div> </div>You provided two examples. One I addressed, and the other was identified as an invalid example. I addressed the former by inquiring whether there was any example of these vampires actually being prevented from taking wounds because of armour worn, in the stories. Is there? In the second case, I asked you to cite fiction - as in written examples in stories - not a reference to another game system. That is why it was invalid.<br /> <br /> Killing a vampire with bullets is not easy in V5, when they only do half, superficial damage and can be healed at will by the vampire each turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-29-2020, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T02:33:52-07:00","id":1384604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384593#post1384593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also saw a ton of vampires wearing armour in the last DA book. But please, inform us, why wouldn't a device specifically designed to deflect or absorb traumatic wounds work at all for vampire? Not that vampires don't really 'need' it, but that it doesn't work for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one's easy, actually. Blades. Those do lethal(agg in v5) without a downgrade to bashing/superficial. Armor (and Fortitude) is the only way to really lessen their damage. Now let's consider what weapons were used in DA, and there's your answer.<br /> <br /> In modern times, this has majorly switched to guns guns guns - or baseball bat stuff. No hueg swords being flailed around. And guns and blunt items only do bashing/superficial, which a vampire yawns at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T04:33:40-07:00","id":1384618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384601#post1384601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that isn\u2019t really an argument. If vampires work like what, they aren\u2019t vampires?<br /> <br /> Vampires are vampires because they are supernatural creatures that feed off blood - which provides them with supernatural power. They are definitely not mortal and, as such, have different qualities to mortals - including their supernatural resistance to lethal damage. Armour designed to protect mortals from lethal damage, accordingly, won\u2019t necessarily be useful to a vampire, in the same respect it wouldn\u2019t be useful to a ghost or Superman.<br /> <br /> You provided two examples. One I addressed, and the other was identified as an invalid example. I addressed the former by inquiring whether there was any example of these vampires actually being prevented from taking wounds because of armour worn, in the stories. Is there? In the second case, I asked you to cite fiction - as in written examples in stories - not a reference to another game system. That is why it was invalid.<br /> <br /> Killing a vampire with bullets is not easy in V5, when they only do half, superficial damage and can be healed at will by the vampire each turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> EDIT: No, actually this is circular, I provided examples, so you move the goalposts and demand more evidence, then completely dismiss how guns and armour actually work...great, you love the system and see no issues, you do you, it completely breaks my immersion to have sheets of armour do nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-29-2020, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T04:46:04-07:00","id":1384621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384618#post1384618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: No, actually this is circular, I provided examples, so you move the goalposts and demand more evidence, then completely dismiss how guns and armour actually work...great, you love the system and see no issues, you do you, it completely breaks my immersion to have sheets of armour do nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I haven\u2019t shifted any goalposts. I actually repeated the same enquiry to you, which you haven\u2019t responded to yet. I don\u2019t think your ideas of immersion are an absolute, which is why we are debating.<br /> <br /> Sheets of armour don\u2019t do \u2019nothing\u2019 - they convert aggravated damage into superficial damage. For vampires, the types of aggravated damage converted is already superficial, so it has little use for them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T05:05:30-07:00","id":1384622,"title":"","content":"But what you're essentially saying <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2517_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2517\" data-vbnamecard=\"2517\">Trippy</a> is that , if we took a vest composed of an inch of kevlar under half an inch of solid steel, which should stop all sorts of anti-personal weaponry on it's own, it shouldn't have any stopping power if a vampire were to wear it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T05:05:46-07:00","id":1384623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384621#post1384621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I haven\u2019t shifted any goalposts. I actually repeated the same enquiry to you, which you haven\u2019t responded to yet. I don\u2019t think your ideas of immersion are an absolute, which is why we are debating.<br /> <br /> Sheets of armour don\u2019t do \u2019nothing\u2019 - they convert aggravated damage into superficial damage. For vampires, the types of aggravated damage converted is already superficial, so it has little use for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> so they do nothing. a .338 lapua does the same damage to a vampire whether it shatters their ribs on the way in and tears their shoulder blade to pieces on the way out, than if it is stopped dead by class 4+ body armour.. dissipating the force over a wide area tell you what, you go through dozens of books to find the explicit statement that armour does not protect vampires at all, after all, that should be stated right? That it magically turns to mist as they wear it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T05:14:14-07:00","id":1384624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384622#post1384622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what you're essentially saying <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2517_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2517\" data-vbnamecard=\"2517\">Trippy</a> is that , if we took a vest composed of an inch of kevlar under half an inch of solid steel, which should stop all sorts of anti-personal weaponry on it's own, it shouldn't have any stopping power if a vampire were to wear it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. No, I\u2019m not saying that. I\u2019m saying that whatever the stopping power of the armour, it would be irrelevant to a vampire that supernaturally has stopping power anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T05:19:54-07:00","id":1384626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384623#post1384623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> so they do nothing. a .338 lapua does the same damage to a vampire whether it shatters their ribs on the way in and tears their shoulder blade to pieces on the way out, than if it is stopped dead by class 4+ body armour.. dissipating the force over a wide area tell you what, you go through dozens of books to find the explicit statement that armour does not protect vampires at all, after all, that should be stated right? That it magically turns to mist as they wear it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The physics is irrelevant. The vampire\u2019s supernatural qualities trump physics in a fictional world. As above, whatever the stopping power of the armour, the vampire already has stopping power so it is irrelevant to them. These factors don\u2019t need to stack - the impact is qualitative not quantitative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T05:26:42-07:00","id":1384628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384624#post1384624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmm. No, I\u2019m not saying that. I\u2019m saying that whatever the stopping power of the armour, it would be irrelevant to a vampire that supernaturally has stopping power anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But the vampire still takes the same amount of damage regardless of if they wear this armour or not. Ergo that thick layer or kevlar and steel are suddenly doing nothing when worn by a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T05:35:39-07:00","id":1384629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384628#post1384628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the vampire still takes the same amount of damage regardless of if they wear this armour or not. Ergo that thick layer or kevlar and steel are suddenly doing nothing when worn by a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because the damage is already rendered superficial. There is no additional benefit from wearing armour for a vampire, in the same manner that Superman or a ghost wouldn\u2019t get any additional benefit. The reason is because they are all supernatural beings whose qualities override natural physics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T05:39:20-07:00","id":1384630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384626#post1384626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The physics is irrelevant. The vampire\u2019s supernatural qualities trump physics in a fictional world. As above, whatever the stopping power of the armour, the vampire already has stopping power so it is irrelevant to them. These factors don\u2019t need to stack - the impact is qualitative not quantitative.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> and that makes absolutely no sense. Vampires are described as taking damage from bullets, in a way far inferior to body armour, in the fiction, tearing flesh, breaking bone etc, and yet, equipment designed to stop those very things happening, does nothing. Still waiting for the page reference for armour being useless, taken from the novels btw, if you expect me to re-read dozens of books seeking 1 sentence, you do that first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T05:40:44-07:00","id":1384631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384629#post1384629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, because the damage is already rendered superficial. There is no additional benefit from wearing armour for a vampire, in the same manner that Superman or a ghost wouldn\u2019t get any additional benefit. The reason is because they are all supernatural beings whose qualities override natural physics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> bullets literally do nothing to Superman. They don't tear his flesh apart, as they do vampires, they don't shatter bones, as they do to vampires, same for the ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T05:51:15-07:00","id":1384633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384630#post1384630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and that makes absolutely no sense. Vampires are described as taking damage from bullets, in a way far inferior to body armour, in the fiction, tearing flesh, breaking bone etc, and yet, equipment designed to stop those very things happening, does nothing. Still waiting for the page reference for armour being useless, taken from the novels btw, if you expect me to re-read dozens of books seeking 1 sentence, you do that first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the example I gave a few pages up shows that a vampires protection (from a shotgun) is not inferior to body armour worn by mortals - it is quite superior to it. And superficial damage means just that - it is not causing tearing flesh, breaking bones or the like <i>to a vampire. </i>When damage is rendered superficial from aggravated, either by a vampire\u2019s supernatural qualities or body armour, it is preventing the damage from being aggravated.<br /> <br /> You shouldn\u2019t really expect me to start giving you references as a response until you provide me with yours first, incidentally - as it merely shows you are deflecting. However, there doesn\u2019t need to be an <i>explicit</i> example of vampires needing to wear armour, inasmuch that it is <i>implicitly</i> demonstrated that hardly any vampires in any literature or movies actually bother with it at all. Like I say, if you check out the 260 or so example characters found in previously published Clanbooks, how many do you think include body armour in their equipment lists?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T05:57:04-07:00","id":1384634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384631#post1384631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">bullets literally do nothing to Superman. They don't tear his flesh apart, as they do vampires, they don't shatter bones, as they do to vampires, same for the ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says that bullets tear flesh or shatter bones of vampires? They don\u2019t. The rules in the book says they don\u2019t - the book says bullets cause <i>superficial damage</i> to vampires. Tearing flesh and breaking bones is <i>aggravated damage, </i>and vampires don\u2019t suffer aggravated damage from bullets. Why? It has nothing to do with physics. Like Superman, vampires are fictional beings whose supernatural powers means that bullets don\u2019t affect them like mortals. So, just like Superman, there isn\u2019t any extra advantage to wearing body armour, which is why they generally don\u2019t. Trenchcoats, possibly. Body armour, unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T06:07:39-07:00","id":1384635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384634#post1384634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who says that bullets tear flesh or shatter bones of vampires? They don\u2019t. The rules in the book says they don\u2019t - the book says bullets cause <i>superficial damage</i> to vampires. Tearing flesh and breaking bones is <i>aggravated damage, </i>and vampires don\u2019t suffer aggravated damage from bullets. Why? It has nothing to do with physics. Like Superman, vampires are fictional beings whose supernatural powers means that bullets don\u2019t affect them like mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> They do. Simply from the description of Los Nueves in the Anarch book we know they rip and tear flesh, perforate and mutilate bodies, destroy faces, shatters bones, etc. Quote Anarch '' His bullet hits me in the face. It hits my upper jaw, sinking bone splinters into the flesh of my mouth'. <br /> <br /> Bone splinters, from, splintered and broken bones....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T06:21:45-07:00","id":1384636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384629#post1384629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, because the damage is already rendered superficial. There is no additional benefit from wearing armour for a vampire, in the same manner that Superman or a ghost wouldn\u2019t get any additional benefit. The reason is because they are all supernatural beings whose qualities override natural physics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 'Rendered' superficial. <br /> <br /> So, the bullet is stopped by the vest, and then the vampire takes damage as if the bullet ripped through him/her. <br /> <br /> Might as well make vampires take damage when the bullets miss them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T06:27:31-07:00","id":1384637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384636#post1384636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 'Rendered' superficial. <br /> <br /> So, the bullet is stopped by the vest, and then the vampire takes damage as if the bullet ripped through him/her. <br /> <br /> Might as well make vampires take damage when the bullets miss them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And as Taggie said, a mortal or ghoul with anti-riot vest receive the same damage that someone naked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T06:48:14-07:00","id":1384639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384635#post1384635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do. Simply from the description of Los Nueves in the Anarch book we know they rip and tear flesh, perforate and mutilate bodies, destroy faces, shatters bones, etc. Quote Anarch '' His bullet hits me in the face. It hits my upper jaw, sinking bone splinters into the flesh of my mouth'.<br /> <br /> Bone splinters, from, splintered and broken bones....</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in this case - using the V5 rules as written - we can assume that the superficial Health levels have been exhausted, causing an Impairment to the vampire, and the excess damage taken is no longer superficial but is now recorded as Aggravated. All in the rules...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T06:49:38-07:00","id":1384641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384639#post1384639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in this case - using the V5 rules as written - we can assume that the superficial Health levels have been exhausted, causing an Impairment to the vampire, and the excess damage taken is no longer superficial but is now recorded as Aggravated. All in the rules...</div> </div> </div> </div>From a single shot? But even so armour could have prevented that type of injury, both from exhausting the superficial levels, and from breaking bone later (tho in this specific case armouring the face is hard)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-29-2020, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T06:52:11-07:00","id":1384643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384636#post1384636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Rendered' superficial.<br /> <br /> So, the bullet is stopped by the vest, and then the vampire takes damage as if the bullet ripped through him/her.<br /> <br /> Might as well make vampires take damage when the bullets miss them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Non sequitur. <br /> <br /> If the bullet is stopped by the vest, and prevented the aggravated damage happening, then the superficial damage of the impact doesn\u2019t stop. The superficial damage on the vampire does not imply that the bullet ripped through him/her. Again, that would be aggravated damage. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T06:54:02-07:00","id":1384644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384641#post1384641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From a single shot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends how good the shot is, and what type of gun/ammo it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T06:55:56-07:00","id":1384645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384637#post1384637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And as Taggie said, a mortal or ghoul with anti-riot vest receive the same damage that someone naked.</div> </div> </div> </div>No they won\u2019t. Any aggravated damage inflicted on a mortal or ghoul with an anti-riot vest will be converted to superficial damage - and half the amount applied to the Health track. A naked person will not get that protection and take the full amount of aggravated wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-29-2020, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T07:07:47-07:00","id":1384648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384644#post1384644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends how good the shot is, and what type of gun/ammo it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>A 9mm Pistol,striking the side of the face with a bullet not noted as special.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T07:07:55-07:00","id":1384649,"title":"","content":"Expecting Realism from a RPG is ridiculous. All RPGs abstract combat. Lets take V20 for instance. Your telling me that taking 3-5 second to land a single punch is realistic. The system doesn't allow you to do anything else without becoming worse at swinging so most people don't they just swing in a slow arch toward the target, that doesn't move by the way, until their fist finally connects or for some reason since your opponent chose not to dodge misses them as you look suprised that your 7 dice pool could do that. Sorry that is not realistic.<br /> <br /> It takes you 3-5 seconds to move 7 to 29 yards on average and no matter how fast you move it has the same effect on someone else aim at you and your ability to shoot another. I can flat out sprint and it will effect my aim the same amount as if I was casually walking toward my non-moving target. but hey when in close combat if I try to stick and move I am gong to be penalized much more than a full out sprint while shooting.<br /> <br /> I can tie a Vampire to a chair rip off his shirt and put a shotgun to his chest and because I would get an automatic hit do potentially less damage to him if at all cause he can soak it all without fortitude given dice. heck I could get 6 net success on my attack place an excellent shot to him in combat and have it do no damage due to damage and soak rolls. no armor no nothing it hits him in the face and nothing.<br /> <br /> I play 20th anniversary games and enjoy them but all systems abstract combat. but hey keep telling yourselves that this isn't a veiled attempt to make V5 look bad because that system that is were the line gets drawn and it has to simulate combat with 100% realism.<br /> <br /> Can we shut this thread down? it serves no purpose but to bash an edition I enjoy playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 04-29-2020, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T07:17:17-07:00","id":1384650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384648#post1384648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A 9mm Pistol,striking the side of the face with a bullet not noted as special.</div> </div> </div> </div>Side of the face - as in superficial damage as it lances by - or to the face causing aggravated trauma? If it is a wound that causes massive trauma, then we might assume a very high level of success on the attack roll, with 00 rolls included. Does the vampire have high Health levels? If the number of successes rolled, plus the bonus 3 from the 9mm adds up to more than the Health levels available, after being halved, then it would inflict an aggravated wound. It would have to be a good shot, but possible. Did the vampire in the fiction survive the shot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T07:25:18-07:00","id":1384651,"title":"","content":"Vampires in fiction tend to take less damage from bullets than a human. I don't just mean they don't die from it, they tend to take neat little holes from bullets that would cause massive injuries to humans. In the case of a bullet to the head, maybe his vampiric nature caused the bullet to make a neat little puncture instead of the near decapitation it would a human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T08:46:01-07:00","id":1384654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384650#post1384650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Side of the face - as in superficial damage as it lances by - or to the face causing aggravated trauma? If it is a wound that causes massive trauma, then we might assume a very high level of success on the attack roll, with 00 rolls included. Does the vampire have high Health levels? If the number of successes rolled, plus the bonus 3 from the 9mm adds up to more than the Health levels available, after being halved, then it would inflict an aggravated wound. It would have to be a good shot, but possible. Did the vampire in the fiction survive the shot?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's directly from the fiction, so rolls aren't mentioned, but it is treated as the shooters 'calling card', the target is fine, a little hungry after healing but that is all, and the shooter does it again to the next person he plays the game against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T09:02:33-07:00","id":1384655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384645#post1384645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they won\u2019t. Any aggravated damage inflicted on a mortal or ghoul with an anti-riot vest will be converted to superficial damage - and half the amount applied to the Health track. A naked person will not get that protection and take the full amount of aggravated wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me fix:<br /> <br /> And as Taggie said, a mortal or ghoul with anti-riot vest receive the same damage from a punch that someone naked","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T10:14:45-07:00","id":1384662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384649#post1384649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I play 20th anniversary games and enjoy them but all systems abstract combat. but hey keep telling yourselves that this isn't a veiled attempt to make V5 look bad because that system that is were the line gets drawn and it has to simulate combat with 100% realism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't expect 100% realism.<br /> But I don't expect the game to take the piss either. Imagine if we changed the game so that guns don't actually hurt people? If armour doesn't actually protect people and only makes a difference in certain circumstances, it's the same as gunshots not hurting people. At the very least, while I'm happy to acknowledge that some rules have to be more abstract to keep the game fast, easy and fluid, it becomes a real problem when my character has to start thinking in accordance to abstractions; &quot;I don't need a bullet proof vest for the upcoming gunfight, it wouldn't grant me a mechanical benefit!&quot;<br /> In my humble opinion; that's where everyone should draw the line. When you can't make intuitive and reasonable decisions within the story's context because the rules say otherwise, your immersion is out the window. Armour providing no protection is tantamount to gunshots doing no damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T11:41:43-07:00","id":1384675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384662#post1384662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't expect 100% realism.<br /> But I don't expect the game to take the piss either. Imagine if we changed the game so that guns don't actually hurt people? If armour doesn't actually protect people and only makes a difference in certain circumstances, it's the same as gunshots not hurting people. At the very least, while I'm happy to acknowledge that some rules have to be more abstract to keep the game fast, easy and fluid, it becomes a real problem when my character has to start thinking in accordance to abstractions; &quot;I don't need a bullet proof vest for the upcoming gunfight, it wouldn't grant me a mechanical benefit!&quot;<br /> In my humble opinion; that's where everyone should draw the line. When you can't make intuitive and reasonable decisions within the story's context because the rules say otherwise, your immersion is out the window. Armour providing no protection is tantamount to gunshots doing no damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't expect realism then why are we in this discussion. Don't sit there and drone on and on about how V5 presents unrealistic armor and then when other systems are pointed to as not real suddenly clam up and say but I don't want to spot light V20s faults I want to just dam V5 and its faults. and yes it is only V5 you talk about because I haven't seen one V20 has unrealistic blah blah blah out of you and your signature speaks volumes of your thoughts.<br /> <br /> Realism? You mean like in V20 were you can put the barrel of a gun to a sleeping vampires head pull the trigger and do no damage due to a bad damage roll and good soak. Is that the line we should draw? I mean by that standard you should never play V20 again, which would be a shame since I like that system as well. I mean yes if we went from a realistic simulation system to an abstract one then draw the line but we are moving from one abstract system with lots of faults to another and nitpicking one change in the abstraction is not only holding that system to an unrealistic high but is an arbitrary asinine line, it is pushing an combative unnecessary agenda. Both have unrealistic abstractions and as your signature suggests and from previous posts you make it very clear you have an agenda to accomplish, it is obvious every time you put another V5 post up.<br /> <br /> You don't say hey I don't like this rule please help me house rule something, which we would gladly do as we all understand no system fits everyone every time, you just come on and start whining or trying to belittle other peoples good times and that is why this is all unacceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 04-29-2020, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T13:01:41-07:00","id":1384686,"title":"","content":"Whut? <br /> If your GM needs you to roll for putting a gun to a sleeping forward, that's the GM's problem. <br /> Please don't criticise me for hating V5. I'm just pointing out things as they are: Armour doesn't approach it's own function. You are defending the indefensible because presumably, you love V5. If one of us was biased, it'd be you. <br /> <br /> You could do armour realistically, or you could do armour in a way that isn't realistic but does in fact seem intuitive and does fit the purpose of armour: Either damage reduction or damage negation or increased difficulty to hit. You could even do a percentage reduction which is hardly realistic, but at least the armour would actually do something. (I think the more realistic, the better, so I'd complain about the percentage reduction, but It would be a lot better than what V5 is offering) In my OP I expressed that I wasn't entirely happy with the way armour was handled in prior editions, something you seem to have selectively ignored because you want to deal in absolutes to make an argument, but the VTM system was a lot more 'realistic' than the V5 system, if not entirely realistic. Sure; a rifle plate wouldn't protect you from a rifle, but at least it would reduce the damage. In V5, a rifle plate won't do anything for you if you're a vampire, and riot gear won't do anything but hinder you if used against weapons common in a riot. If VTM was 'bad', V5 is &quot;terrible&quot; because armour doesn't actually do anything outside of some very speific niches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T13:34:32-07:00","id":1384690,"title":"","content":"*sigh* Do you really want games where vampires are running around armored up like the Michelin Man instead of in cool &quot;Underworld&quot; style outfights?<br /> Y'know, two of my favorite classes to play in D&amp;D are Monks and Barbarians. Barbarians are, somehow, tougher running around bare-chested than they would be in armor. Is it realistic? No. I don't care, because I want to play a class that is tough as hell running around bare-chested. So I happily suspend disbelief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T13:44:09-07:00","id":1384691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384686#post1384686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whut?<br /> If your GM needs you to roll for putting a gun to a sleeping forward, that's the GM's problem.<br /> Please don't criticise me for hating V5. I'm just pointing out things as they are: Armour doesn't approach it's own function. You are defending the indefensible because presumably, you love V5. If one of us was biased, it'd be you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say roll to put the gun to his head I said damage and soak rolls their is no coupe de gras in V20 that I have seen only automatic hits which is another problem with the system. why is it when the shot is easier I have less chance at getting better damage. this is completely against the way it should work int he real world. Attack rolls simulate the quality of the shot but in V20 if the shot is too easy you automatically succeed and get no net success increasing the chance that it will do no damage after Damage and soak rolls.<br /> <br /> An no I'm not biased I play two 20th anniversary games one of which I run and 2 V5 games. Up until recently I played exclusivly Revised and Chronicles. I love all of the Storyteller systems and play in many of them. I don't run around starting threads with an obvious anti system bent nor put in my signature line a biased confrontational opinion.<br /> <br /> As far as criticism goes if someone is allowed to criticize a companies work then those criticisms are up for scrutiny as well. My point which still has not been countered is ALL systems are unrealistic and one system use of abstraction does not make that system worse because of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384686#post1384686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could do armour realistically, or you could do armour in a way that isn't realistic but does in fact seem intuitive and does fit the purpose of armour: Either damage reduction or damage negation or increased difficulty to hit. You could even do a percentage reduction which is hardly realistic, but at least the armour would actually do something. (I think the more realistic, the better, so I'd complain about the percentage reduction, but It would be a lot better than what V5 is offering) In my OP I expressed that I wasn't entirely happy with the way armour was handled in prior editions, something you seem to have selectively ignored because you want to deal in absolutes to make an argument, but the VTM system was a lot more 'realistic' than the V5 system, if not entirely realistic. Sure; a rifle plate wouldn't protect you from a rifle, but at least it would reduce the damage. In V5, a rifle plate won't do anything for you if you're a vampire, and riot gear won't do anything but hinder you if used against weapons common in a riot. If VTM was 'bad', V5 is &quot;terrible&quot; because armor doesn't actually do anything outside of some very speific niches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you can do armor more realistically but it is not singular to this system. in D&amp;D why is it that armor makes you harder to hit, not damage but hit. because it is an abstraction that's why. In V20 why is it the armor can stop a stick of dynamite stuck down your pants from blowing your nether region off, abstraction that is why. and yes why in V5 does armor not give extra to vampires abstraction that is why. No system is immune to it, no system is perfect, but you feel that it has to be or damn the world. It has been said several times that systems have abstraction but that is not the take away that is not acceptable to you lot because what is actually at the heart of this discussion it is that V5 bad, everything else good.<br /> <br /> When known anti-V5 players try to help and give you new systems or pro-V5 people try to give houserules you would think that you would go &quot;yea games do that, how can we make a better rule?&quot; and move the F on. But no, that is not the agenda here that is not acceptable. That's on you not my GM or me, its on you. You have chosen to not accept anything but the admission that &quot;V5 is not VtM&quot;<br /> <br /> I am not saying V5 is all golddust and rainbows but what I am saying is, it is no different than any other game system on the market. If you don't like it fine ask for a helpful houserule to change it but move on or play something else. because listening to this day after day for what, almost 2 years now is enough. every week there is someone on discord complaining about how these forums are a toxic cesspool of hate and TBH I for one don't like that. I don't like hearing or feeling like &quot;our kind is not welcome here.&quot; I don't like knowing that i can't come on here and get a halfway decent conversation in a form for discussion that I choose to like, without you or someone else coming along and pissing in my cheerios, I've already went through that back in the end of time days and I don't want to do it again.<br /> <br /> So as long as you continue to try and veil your contempt in a negative manor I will criticize your comments. Until I get doxed or banned. and after this post I could see it happening. I think I will try and take a couple days off again.<br /> <br /> Sorry <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> If I cross a line please let me know though this post seems counter to the opinion I don not want to make these boards hostile to those that wish to be here in mutual love of the WoD and all of its editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 04-29-2020, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T13:54:10-07:00","id":1384693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384691#post1384691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not saying V5 is all golddust and rainbows but what I am saying is, it is no different than any other game system on the market. If you don't like it fine ask for a helpful houserule to change it but move on or play something else. because listening to this day after day for what, almost 2 years now is enough. every week there is someone on discord complaining about how these forums are a toxic cesspool of hate and TBH I for one don't like that. I don't like hearing or feeling like &quot;our kind is not welcome here.&quot; I don't like knowing that i can't come on here and get a halfway decent conversation in a form for discussion that I choose to like, without you or someone else coming along and pissing in my cheerios, I've already went through that back in the end of time days and I don't want to do it again.<br /> <br /> So as long as you continue to try and veil your contempt in a negative manor I will criticize your comments. Until I get doxed or banned. and after this post I could see it happening. I think I will try and take a couple days off again.<br /> <br /> Sorry <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11720_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11720\" data-vbnamecard=\"11720\">Redwulfe</a>, the point I have been trying to get across is the fact that it is not the job of posters to police the forum. The toxicity you reference is a thing that has badly tainted the community around here where people who hate V5 for whatever reason (Sabbat, Anarchs, Humanity, Touchstones, art) get into fights with those who want to defend it. I've been guilty of that sort of thing myself. However, the simple fact it is up to the moderators to say when someone is being hostile or threadcrapping. Which is to say if people have a problem with someone's post they should use the Flag button and report a post. It's not their job to play sheriff and it just contributes to things getting worse.<br /> <br /> Personal attacks will get banned. Be they on fellow posters or the developers. People have a right to say they don't like something but I'll be trying to make sure the tone remains civil and everyone remembers that the no. 1# rule here, &quot;we're all fans of Vampire: The Masquerade here. We're here to talk about our hobby with people who love the same thing we do.&quot; I intend to show no favoritism on this, both V20 and V5 fans are welcome here.<br /> <br /> Please trust me to do my job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T13:55:40-07:00","id":1384694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384690#post1384690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*sigh* Do you really want games where vampires are running around armored up like the Michelin Man instead of in cool &quot;Underworld&quot; style outfights?<br /> Y'know, two of my favorite classes to play in D&amp;D are Monks and Barbarians. Barbarians are, somehow, tougher running around bare-chested than they would be in armor. Is it realistic? No. I don't care, because I want to play a class that is tough as hell running around bare-chested. So I happily suspend disbelief.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's totally your prerogative. if you wanna go fight naked, more power to you. I too am a sucker for Rolo'ing my way through enemies not needing armour. In-fact, I'm pretty sure if you wore armour in WTA: I'd make you lose honour, unless you were a glass walker in which case I'd shout at you for not mech-ing yourself up. <b>I don't have any problem with you wanting to play an unarmoured badass; but should that really stop me from playing an armoured badass?</b> Do you hate Fighters and paladins? Do you never armour your barbarian? It's entirely possible to have armoured and unarmoured players, but V5, in denying armour it's purpose, sets everyone up to be run'n gun underworld/matrix fighters. And whilst you might like that, wouldn't it be better if everyone could have fun? Maybe I want to john-wick/Frank Castle/Terminator my way through my enemies? (Yeah, that latter isn't really armoured, but he is made of steel)<br /> <br /> Modern armour doesn't actually necessitate you to look like the michalin man either. There's concealable body armour, some of it's really good. But the point is: just because your vision of how you want to fight is fulfilled doesn't mean that it's good that other people have their visions denied. In VTM, you could wear armour or blood buff yourself to madness to make up for a lack of Fortitude, you could gain Fortitude so you don't need armour, and you could wear armour with your Fortitude to become an absolute tank. There was no wrong way to play. But Now, if you want your vampire to wear armour, you're a badwrongfun powergamer or something and as such armour will not do anything for you...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-29-2020, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T13:57:35-07:00","id":1384695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384655#post1384655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me fix:<br /> <br /> And as Taggie said, a mortal or ghoul with anti-riot vest receive the same damage from a punch that someone naked</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven\u2019t fixed anything. We were talking specifically about bullets in the previous example. So your shifting of the example is disingenuous. <br /> <br /> And, correct, any mortal person who is punched will not receive any special protection from body armour because a punch is superficial damage already - and body armour merely converts aggravated damage into superficial damage. This a strain argument, because nobody argued against this point before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:02:14-07:00","id":1384697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384654#post1384654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's directly from the fiction, so rolls aren't mentioned, but it is treated as the shooters 'calling card', the target is fine, a little hungry after healing but that is all, and the shooter does it again to the next person he plays the game against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, so if the character healed immediately, and the impact of the bullet didn\u2019t have any impairment effect, then we can assume it was superficial damage to the vampire and the described blood splatter was merely artistic license in the telling of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:09:39-07:00","id":1384699,"title":"","content":"Speaking as a fan:<br /> <br /> My opinion on body armor is that it should be something that is more useful to mortals than it is for vampires but it should be able to add just a little in the way of protection. Vampires don't have functional organs for the most part and don't bleed so bullets don't do the same sort of damage they do to normal people.<br /> <br /> So, maybe a kevlar vest would add +1 or +2 but not nearly as much benefit to a mortal, which would allow a different kind of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:10:48-07:00","id":1384700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\">MyWifeIsScary</a></b><b>]I don't have any problem with you wanting to play an unarmoured badass; but should that really stop me from playing an armoured badass?</b> Do you hate Fighters and paladins? Do you never armour your barbarian? It's entirely possible to have armoured and unarmoured players, but V5, in denying armour it's purpose, sets everyone up to be run'n gun underworld/matrix fighters. And whilst you might like that, wouldn't it be better if everyone could have fun? Maybe I want to john-wick/Frank Castle/Terminator my way through my enemies? (Yeah, that latter isn't really armoured, but he is made of steel) </div> </div> </div>Actually, it may just be to stop people playing the game as if it was D&amp;D, and cannot get out of the mentality that Vampire is a game where you are not trying to play D&amp;D with it. Vampire isn\u2019t D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> The Vampire game is not, in fact, designed so that everybody can have fun with it. Indeed, a whole lot of people will not have fun even contemplating playing a vampire in a world of darkness setting. It has, as a game, a very specific premise and market thereof. It is not up to the game designers or anybody else to create a game compromises that vision or to change that vision because somebody doesn\u2019t like it. If you want to do it with your own games that is fine.<br /> <br /> If a Barbarian wears armour in D&amp;D, by the way, they lose their 'natural protection' in the rules - so wearing armour is often quite negligible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:33:21-07:00","id":1384704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384700#post1384700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it may just be to stop people playing the game as if it was D&amp;D, and cannot get out of the mentality that Vampire is a game where you are not trying to play D&amp;D with it. Vampire isn\u2019t D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> The Vampire game is not, in fact, designed so that everybody can have fun with it. Indeed, a whole lot of people will not have fun even contemplating playing a vampire in a world of darkness setting. It has, as a game, a very specific premise and market thereof. It is not up to the game designers or anybody else to create a game compromises that vision or to change that vision because somebody doesn\u2019t like it. If you want to do it with your own games that is fine.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aye, VTM is supposed to be a setting where it's our world but with supernaturals. A dark, gritty reality where everything's shit, just like the real world but confirmed by the authors.<br /> What's that got against armour? Vampire has never said &quot;look at underworld, Be underworld! Go dress in leather and dual wield submachineguns!&quot; If anything, Vampire has said &quot;Let's launch a series of home invasions in order to take out the prince's supporters. Time to carefully plan our approach and ensure we don't take losses&quot;. Your interpretation seems to be a lot more fantastical than mine. <br /> <br /> If it's not explicitly magical, it's mundane, and armour works just fine as mundane. It just seems like you've disembowled a chicken to look at it's guts and now know the words of the gods. Why doesn't armour work? What's the thematic benefit of not having armour work? What's the satiric benefit of armour not working? Have the masters of the word descended from the heavens to tell us that armour doesn't work with the holy 'gothic punk' ? What's thy drug of choice? What have thy got? What is this premise, which eludes common sense, that says the laws of physics should be suspended so that armour shouldn't work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:42:28-07:00","id":1384706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384697#post1384697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, so if the character healed immediately, and the impact of the bullet didn\u2019t have any impairment effect, then we can assume it was superficial damage to the vampire and the described blood splatter was merely artistic license in the telling of the story.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> but it's damage that armour would and could have prevented. No shattered jaw, no broken teeth, just the thud of a round striking trauma plate, and the blow of the plate dissipating the energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:43:29-07:00","id":1384707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384700#post1384700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, it may just be to stop people playing the game as if it was D&amp;D, and cannot get out of the mentality that Vampire is a game where you are not trying to play D&amp;D with it. Vampire isn\u2019t D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> The Vampire game is not, in fact, designed so that everybody can have fun with it. Indeed, a whole lot of people will not have fun even contemplating playing a vampire in a world of darkness setting. It has, as a game, a very specific premise and market thereof. It is not up to the game designers or anybody else to create a game compromises that vision or to change that vision because somebody doesn\u2019t like it. If you want to do it with your own games that is fine.<br /> <br /> If a Barbarian wears armour in D&amp;D, by the way, they lose their 'natural protection' in the rules - so wearing armour is often quite negligible.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> but the vision of V5 in Underworld and Anarchs...totally counter to the previous editions the vision has been discarded already, we just want some of it back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:48:02-07:00","id":1384709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384704#post1384704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aye, VTM is supposed to be a setting where it's our world but with supernaturals. A dark, gritty reality where everything's shit, just like the real world but confirmed by the authors.<br /> What's that got against armour? Vampire has never said &quot;look at underworld, Be underworld! Go dress in leather and dual wield submachineguns!&quot; If anything, Vampire has said &quot;Let's launch a series of home invasions in order to take out the prince's supporters. Time to carefully plan our approach and ensure we don't take losses&quot;. Your interpretation seems to be a lot more fantastical than mine.<br /> <br /> If it's not explicitly magical, it's mundane, and armour works just fine as mundane. It just seems like you've disembowled a chicken to look at it's guts and now know the words of the gods. Why doesn't armour work? What's the thematic benefit of not having armour work? What's the satiric benefit of armour not working? Have the masters of the word descended from the heavens to tell us that armour doesn't work with the holy 'gothic punk' ? What's thy drug of choice? What have thy got? What is this premise, which eludes common sense, that says the laws of physics should be suspended so that armour shouldn't work?</div> </div> </div> </div>You actually manage to spin all of this out of a single rule about body armour?!<br /> <br /> The fundamental premise that you are arguing - that armour doesn\u2019t work - is wrong. It does work - it protects against aggravated damage. As far as the rules go, it does exactly what it says on the tin. Everything else just spins out of this incorrect premise. There is no underlying satire to it, or implication over the style of the game. It is just a single rule about armour that you don\u2019t like, and frankly it is just an act of trolling to try and pretend otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:50:49-07:00","id":1384710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384706#post1384706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it's damage that armour would and could have prevented. No shattered jaw, no broken teeth, just the thud of a round striking trauma plate, and the blow of the plate dissipating the energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said he healed it, and presumably in the same scene. That is, there was no impairment or lingering damage to the vampire. Make up your mind.<br /> <br /> If he healed it immediately, it was superficial damage to the vampire with a bit of written flourish for dramatic effect. If he was physically impaired by the shot, and the wounds lingered, then it was aggravated damage. Armour wouldn\u2019t;t have made a difference if it was superficial, and wouldn\u2019t have made a difference if it was a highly accurate shot either, with exceptional dice rolling, in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-29-2020, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T14:57:06-07:00","id":1384712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384710#post1384710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said he healed it, and presumably in the same scene. That is, there was no impairment or lingering damage to the vampire. Make up your mind.<br /> <br /> If he healed it immediately, it was superficial damage to the vampire with a bit of written flourish for dramatic effect. If he was physically impaired by the shot, and the wounds lingered, then it was aggravated damage. Armour wouldn\u2019t;t have made a difference if it was superficial, and wouldn\u2019t have made a difference if it was a highly accurate shot either, with exceptional dice rolling, in fact.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But IT SHOULD HAVE. Stop using bad mechanics to justify themselves, that is a circular argument and doesn't actually prove anything. The fact that all armor does is something vampires already do is the exact problem. It is not 'flourish for dramatic effect' it is shattered bone and blasted flesh, which armour could have prevented, you know, as armour actually does, the rioters example against police, you punch aq guy in real riot armour, all that happens is you break your hand, a baseball bat may hurt...may, but it takes effort to break that stuff, something this system fails to represent, again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:04:04-07:00","id":1384714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384699#post1384699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as a fan:<br /> <br /> My opinion on body armor is that it should be something that is more useful to mortals than it is for vampires but it should be able to add just a little in the way of protection. Vampires don't have functional organs for the most part and don't bleed so bullets don't do the same sort of damage they do to normal people.<br /> <br /> So, maybe a kevlar vest would add +1 or +2 but not nearly as much benefit to a mortal, which would allow a different kind of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me nerd out for a bit: From someone interested in the subject, it'd actually be <i>more useful. </i> Physically, not just because of the masquerade benefit. Especially considering &quot;dark ages&quot; armour.<br /> <br /> A vampire doesn't need their organs and can't bleed to death form a wound, but they need to avoid getting ripped apart because a massive amount of damage will still lead to their final death. We could say Vampires are pretty good against penetrating attacks (stabs, rifles) and resistant against blunt force trauma; but they're weak to relatively wide area attacks like chops and shotguns turning them into spaghetti. Armour, coincidentally is really great at dealing with those spread out attacks like slashes and shotgun pelets; Even if kevlar is almost useless for stabs and with high velocity rifles, it's still really tough against slashing attacks and buckshot. If you go back in time to full-plate, a vampire is almost invincible. You need absolutely massive force to get through full plate armour, you absolutely can't slash at it unless you're using a poleaxe or something excessive. Your best bet at fighting someone with full-plate, if you don't have a powerful gun (which, again, vampires are pretty resistant to those deep and narrow wounds) is to stab through the gaps of the armour; But then you arive at the problem: you're dealing with a vampire. A common way with dealing with medieval knights was to somehow get them on the ground and then put a slim dagger through their eye slit or in a gap at their neck, or their armpit; What's that going to do to a vampire? You can put your dagger through the eye and the brain and they'd still be trying to kill you. You can't just decapitate the vampire because there's too much armour at the neck, you can't just cut off a limb because those are protected well. You can do small damages, but the vampire can heal those during combat. Your only choice with a vampire wearing full armour would be to have teammates and smash the vampire with a hammer repeatedly, praying they don't have fortitude. Maybe if you dent the armour in enough it'll stop the leech from heailing. Vampires also don't need to breath, which is really beneficial for wearing a lot of armour and for wearing modern concealable armour. In modern times, when you get shot in armour, there's often some deformation at the back face of the armour and you still get a big punch from this even if the bullet is stopped: I don't think this would actually be a problem with a vampire because you don't need to breath and don't need all your ribs, and all this is before considering Fortitude. Having armour limits the kinds of attacks that can be made against you and limits where the attacks can go.<br /> <br /> Considering what we know of vampire physiology, Armour would give vampires an even bigger advantage than it would mortals. Of course, mortals benefit more since armour would save their life whilst for vampires it would just multiply their resiliency, but the advantages for a vampire can't be understated. The only problem with vampires wearing armour is a social one; &quot;<i>Just what do you think is going to happen to this elysium?</i>&quot; &quot;<i>what you doing with all that gear, son?&quot; </i> &quot;<i>Going to school, are we?&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 04-29-2020, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:08:54-07:00","id":1384716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384704#post1384704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's not explicitly magical, it's mundane, and armour works just fine as mundane. It just seems like you've disembowled a chicken to look at it's guts and now know the words of the gods. Why doesn't armour work? What's the thematic benefit of not having armour work? What's the satiric benefit of armour not working? Have the masters of the word descended from the heavens to tell us that armour doesn't work with the holy 'gothic punk' ? What's thy drug of choice? What have thy got? What is this premise, which eludes common sense, that says the laws of physics should be suspended so that armour shouldn't work?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the setting conceits behind it are:<br /> - Bullets don't affect vampires very much, because bullets generally kill people via bleeding or organ damage, neither of which matters to a vampire.<br /> - Blunt impacts affect vampires about as much as they affect humans.<br /> <br /> This is why, in all the editions I can think of (maybe even back to 1e? I don't have the 1e book with me to check), shooting a vampire does bashing, shooting a mortal does lethal, punching a vampire does bashing, punching a mortal does bashing. (Vampires are also more resilient to punches than mortals are, sure, but that comes from rapid healing and Fortitude, not intrinsic downgrading.)<br /> <br /> The devs then said, well, if the main benefit of a bulletproof vest is that it turns a bullet wound into a blunt impact, and bullets and blunt impacts affect vampires about equally (they're both bashing damage), then <b>it would make sense in-universe</b> that armor doesn't really help vampires at all. The main benefit is preventing the bleeding and organ damage from a bullet wound, and <b>vampires are already immune to those things</b>.<br /> <br /> It's not the armor magically becomes permeable when a vampire wears it. It's that armor turns one type of damage into another, but those two types of damage are pretty much equivalent to a vampire anyway, so there's not much benefit to having a broken rib instead of a bullet in your abdomen. Flavorfully they look different, but mechanically they're both bashing damage on the sheet. Because bashing versus lethal versus aggravated (or superficial versus aggravated) is just an abstraction, representing how much of a problem the damage is and how hard it'll be to heal.<br /> <br /> <b>All that said</b>, I do think it would make sense to go into more detail on what protects from what. Different types of armor should protect you from different things, and some of those things would be useful to a vampire, even if a bulletproof vest wouldn't. And it would also make sense to have rules for armor absorbing the damage rather than just converting it, like ceramic trauma plates shattering. <b>I agree completely on that front.</b> But the hyperbole about &quot;this premise, which eludes common sense, that says the laws of physics should be suspended so that armour shouldn't work&quot; is getting tiring. The reasoning behind this has been part of the game ever since long before V5. Yes, maybe the existence of undead vampires defies biology. I don't particularly care. &quot;Vampires exist and work like this&quot; is one of the premises of the setting, and &quot;vampires take bashing from bullets because they don't need their organs&quot; is too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:10:26-07:00","id":1384719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384714#post1384714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering what we know of vampire physiology, Armour would give vampires an even bigger advantage than it would mortals. Of course, mortals benefit more since armour would save their life whilst for vampires it would just multiply their resiliency, but the advantages for a vampire can't be understated. The only problem with vampires wearing armour is a social one; &quot;<i>Just what do you think is going to happen to this elysium?</i>&quot; &quot;<i>what you doing with all that gear, son?&quot; </i> &quot;<i>Going to school, are we?&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You're probably correct, though I imagine the only people who would be wearing body armor in that respect are vampires expecting attack like Archons or Paladins. The majority of undead enter combat unexpectedly due to the Masquerade and getting ambushed rather than wearing it in their day to day lives. So, yes, you are correct but it's also something that most vampires won't be possessing anymore than they do automatic weapons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:13:07-07:00","id":1384720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384714#post1384714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We could say Vampires are pretty good against penetrating attacks (stabs, rifles) and resistant against blunt force trauma; but they're weak to relatively wide area attacks like chops and shotguns turning them into spaghetti. Armour, coincidentally is really great at dealing with those spread out attacks like slashes and shotgun pelets; Even if kevlar is almost useless for stabs and with high velocity rifles, it's still really tough against slashing attacks and buckshot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! And I agree, some rules for dealing with different types of damage sources would be nice, and I hope the Player's Guide has them. To take it to extremes, even if vampires don't need to be particularly scared of pistol bullets, they should be <i>very</i> scared of fire, and equipment that can help protect against that makes perfect sense (and can't really be represented in the current rules).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:15:14-07:00","id":1384722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384712#post1384712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But IT SHOULD HAVE. Stop using bad mechanics to justify themselves, that is a circular argument and doesn't actually prove anything. The fact that all armor does is something vampires already do is the exact problem. It is not 'flourish for dramatic effect' it is shattered bone and blasted flesh, which armour could have prevented, you know, as armour actually does, the rioters example against police, you punch aq guy in real riot armour, all that happens is you break your hand, a baseball bat may hurt...may, but it takes effort to break that stuff, something this system fails to represent, again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Writing in capitals does nothing to improve your argument. These are not bad mechanics just because you don\u2019t like or get them.<br /> <br /> If somebody immediately heals the effects, by magical means as you seem to have argued, then the game effect is nil. The narrator is allowed to describe events for dramatic effect however. The system is abstracted to allow for dramatic descriptions - rather than being a simulationist system. <br /> <br /> In the real world, riot armour does act to protect against lethal damage, but the wearer can still suffer bruises and superficial damage after using it in conflict. An attack doesn\u2019t have to be just punching, it could be pushing them to the ground, kicking, stamping, biting, whatever. The system is abstracted - so the success of an attack could be interpreted in any narrative way seen fit to account for damage occurring. A baseball bat may hurt (superficial) against an armoured person, but it could cause major trauma (aggravated) without - so the armour is essentially converting aggravated damage into superficial damage as per the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:18:28-07:00","id":1384724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384719#post1384719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're probably correct, though I imagine the only people who would be wearing body armor in that respect are vampires expecting attack like Archons or Paladins. The majority of undead enter combat unexpectedly due to the Masquerade and getting ambushed rather than wearing it in their day to day lives. So, yes, you are correct but it's also something that most vampires won't be possessing anymore than they do automatic weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which is fine, it shouldn't be 'everyone is in class 4 at all times' (which btw is surprisingly cheap, and no I don't own any, was looking for surplus kit of camping and body armour was available on the site), but a Templar or an Archon should be able to rock you world when they roll in geared for war, mortal technology and supernatural might in absolutely horrifying synergy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:21:13-07:00","id":1384725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384716#post1384716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why, in all the editions I can think of (maybe even back to 1e? I don't have the 1e book with me to check), shooting a vampire does bashing, shooting a mortal does lethal, punching a vampire does bashing, punching a mortal does bashing. (Vampires are also more resilient to punches than mortals are, sure, but that comes from rapid healing and Fortitude, not intrinsic downgrading.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The actual differentiation between damage types wasn\u2019t introduced till Vampire: Revised came out, actually. In Vampire 1st, the combat section was brief - about five pages long - and worked a bit more abstractly than later editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-29-2020, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:21:16-07:00","id":1384726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384722#post1384722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Writing in capitals does nothing to improve your argument. These are not bad mechanics just because you don\u2019t like or get them.<br /> <br /> If somebody immediately heals the effects, by magical means as you seem to have argued, then the game effect is nil. The narrator is allowed to describe events for dramatic effect however. The system is abstracted to allow for dramatic descriptions - rather than being a simulationist system.<br /> <br /> In the real world, riot armour does act to protect against lethal damage, but the wearer can still suffer bruises and superficial damage after using it in conflict. An attack doesn\u2019t have to be just punching, it could be pushing them to the ground, kicking, stamping, biting, whatever. The system is abstracted - so the success of an attack could be interpreted in any narrative way seen fit to account for damage occurring. A baseball bat may hurt (superficial) against an armoured person, but it could cause major trauma (aggravated) without - so the armour is essentially converting aggravated damage into superficial damage as per the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> and again you use mechanics that ignore the fiction in their own books to justify those same mechanics....how is that supposed to work? Because right now they don't at all. (Even the advanced combat barely qualifies as a system for instance)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:23:27-07:00","id":1384728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless?p=1384726#post1384726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and again you use mechanics that ignore the fiction in their own books to justify those same mechanics....how is that supposed to work? Because right now they don't at all. (Even the advanced combat barely qualifies as a system for instance)</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m just going on your own account of the fiction you selected to recount, but the fundamental disconnect you are having in all of this is you don\u2019t seem to accept that the game system is abstracted - and the effects of any given outcome can be described by the storyteller any way they feel fit to add drama to the occasion.<br /> <br /> The advanced combat, as well as the basic conflict resolution, both qualify as systems in V5. A system is just a standardized way of doing things. Just because you don\u2019t like the system, doesn\u2019t mean it doesn\u2019t qualify as a system.<br /> <br /> The V5 is attempting to make systems that are abstracted for the purpose of narrative design. Maybe, the Players Guide will add other systems with other priorities - like grid maps and tactical wargaming, for example. We know there is a miniature line along the way....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-29-2020, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T01:41:19-07:00","id":1384806,"title":"","content":"When armour gets shot, it's not like every KJ of force still travels into the occupant. A good amount is absorbed and dispersed by the vest. If you're wearing something very protective and get hit by something relatively small, there's good odds that you won't even notice you're hit, whilst if we're talking about a bullet that slightly exceeds the limitations of what a vest is designed to recieve without penetration, you might actually be looking at something which, in VTM terms would be... 1-3 <i>lethal</i> damage. Because that bullet might as well be a warhammer and the internal injuries will kill somebody. But unless players are going around with anti-material rifles or bear-hunting cartridges, you're not really in that territory. If you shoot someone in military body armour with a big-but-expected 7.62 Nato round, they might get knocked to the floor, they might be shocked, they might be bruised, but it's not 'damage' territory insofar as wound penalties should start applying. If you shot at a cop with .22LR whilst they wore a duty vest, they might not even notice they've been shot, but they'd probably notice 9mm, and if you shot the soldier with 9mm, they'd maybe not notice this (Obviously, I haven't tested this stuff myself and I'm ball-parking, but I should be close to accurate if not accurate) And yet, in V5, If I'm wearing military body armour, I'd still recieve a 22LR shot as if I was wearing light police gear or if i was a vampire, as if I was wearing nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T01:53:15-07:00","id":1384807,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that just broke the boredom threshold. I\u2019m out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T09:04:43-07:00","id":1384849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1383665-v5-armour-is-useless#post1383665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, prior editions had plenty of problems with armour. In some ways better than reality (Thick clothes are wonderful) and in other ways far worse (A kevlar vest protects for 3 but a common small pistol <i>starts</i> at 4 damage? The best armour protects for only 5 or 6?)<br /> <br /> I can see why it's like that, even if I don't like the reasoning I can see why it's done, and players still have incentive to obtain armour (providing they're willing to take on those ludicrus dex penalties)<br /> <br /> <br /> But in V5<br /> Armour is functionally paper for vampires. Ok, Maybe it works to take the kick out of incindiary rounds, but a plate carrier filled with steel becomes a cheap fabric shirt so long as it's donned by a vampire. Don't argue that vampires don't need armour because they're tough and undead. That's like saying a castle shouldn't benefit from walls if it's on a hill. It just seems rather unfair and breaks a lot of versmillitude for me. I was wondering if people house rule V5 armour heavily or if you're happy with these 'cinematic' rules.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it was one of the issues, rules-wise, that turned me off in V5 (and I wrote about it at length back then, several times). Yes, it's bollocks and said to me a lot about what kind of game the writers intended it to be, which is not one I'm particularly interested playing. I just want more &quot;realistic simulation&quot; and more detailed combat rules in the game and V5 isn't doing that. <br /> <br /> Naturally, not everybody's concerned about things like this, or other rules that breaks verisimilitude for me. That's fine, tastes differ. I know what kind of games and rules system I like and V5 doesn't match that.<br /> <br /> Funnily (or not :/ ), Shadowrun 6 displayed some of the same issues. Pixies having the same damage with an axe as a troll, because Str doesn't contribute to melee weapon damage. Armor not giving damage reduction. Looks like it's somewhat of a fad these days, but it just turns me off of these games. Good thing I have the prior editions.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd just say, support V20 (and the other 20ths). Buy V20 products, if you can. If you have all of them, buy high-quality STsVault books from trusted, long-time WoD authors, written for V20. You don't <i>have </i>to play the latest edition. We're currently playing D&amp;D 3.5, because 5e proved to be too simplified for us and we're playing the 3e Forgotten Realms, because everybody hated the Spellplague and what came after. I'm buying 3.5 books I couldn't back then and having tremendous fun homebrewing a lot for the system. Same with WoD and SR (which I'll still buy 6e plot and other fluff books). I'll buy Technocracy Reloaded, and the remaining 20th books. I won't buy V5, or other 5th books as long as things remain the same, regarding direction. Not in spite, but because they simply don't meet my taste and my vision of WoD.<br /> <br /> I skipped editions of games I love earlier. I skipped D&amp;D 4e completely. I skipped most of NWoD, though I liked several things about it, like the core human books and Hunter, all-in-all, it couldn't compare for the classic WoD for me. I'd rather feel excited about the new stuff, but it is how it is. While it's not great, it's not the end of the world either. <br /> <br /> So, play V20. Introduce new people to V20 and the classic setting. Buy V20 products. Vote with your wallet and leg. Hopefully, the next edition will be more to our tastes.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}